INFO 03-13 07:53:39 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-95a10167fc814cd18e6f59c5fb552b09-0: prompt: 'Here is the function with the name `foo` changed to a more descriptive name:\n```\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    """\n    Returns True if n is prime, False otherwise.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    n: An integer.\n    \n    Returns:\n    A boolean indicating whether n is prime.\n    """\n    # Check if n is prime\n    if n > 2:\n        # Iterate over the range 2 to the square root of n, plus 1\n        for i in range(2, int(n ** 0.5) + 1):\n            # If n is divisible by i, it is not prime\n            if not n % i:\n                return False\n        # If n was not divisible by any number in the range, it is prime\n        return True\n    # Handle the special case of n being 2, the smallest prime number\n    elif n == 2:\n        return True\n    # All other values of n are not prime\n    else:\n        return False\n    \n    \ndef get_primes(l: list) -> list:\n    """\n    Returns a list of prime numbers from the input list.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    l: A list of integers.\n    \n    Returns:\n    A list of prime numbers from the input list.\n    """\n    # Initialize an empty list to store the prime numbers\n    primes = []\n    \n    # Iterate over the input list\n    for item in l:\n        # If the item is prime, append it to the list of primes\n        if is_prime(item):\n            primes.append(item)\n    \n    # Return the list of prime numbers\n    return primes\n```\nThe function `foo` has been renamed to `get_primes`, which is a more descriptive and self-explanatory name that better reflects the purpose of the function. This makes the code easier to understand and use, as the function\'s name provides a clear indication of its behavior.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], inclu