INFO 03-13 07:53:44 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-4402edd3e54a45118113b51e952969d4-0: prompt: 'The cross is undoubtedly the most recognizable and significant symbol in Christianity, evoking powerful emotions and inspiring deep contemplation in believers and non-believers alike. Its origins, however, predate Christianity and can be traced back to ancient civilizations and cultures that used it as a religious symbol long before the birth of Christ.\n\nDespite its varied historical roots, the cross has come to be strongly associated with the crucifixion of Jesus Christ, who died on a wooden cross to atone for the sins of humanity. This association has imbued the cross with deep meaning in Christianity, symbolizing salvation, redemption, and eternal life through faith in Christ.\n\nOver time, the cross has taken on different forms and meanings within Christianity, including the Latin cross, the Celtic cross, and the Orthodox cross. It has also been used in various ways, such as on altars, as a jewelry accessory, and as a part of religious ceremonies.\n\nHowever, the cross\'s association with violence and persecution throughout history has made it a controversial symbol in some circles. Nevertheless, the cross remains a potent and deeply meaningful symbol in Christianity.\n\nManly P. Hall, a prominent 20th-century scholar of philosophy and symbolism, wrote extensively about the origins of the cross in his book, "The Secret Teachings of All Ages." According to Hall, the cross has deep roots in human history and was originally a symbol of the sun, representing the four cardinal directions and the four seasons.\n\nIn addition to its solar symbolism, Hall argued that the cross represented the intersection of the spiritual and material worlds. The point where the two intersected symbolized the meeting place of heaven and earth, or the union of the spiritual and material aspects of human existence.\n\nFor Hall, the cross was also a potent symbol in the mystery schools of ancient times, where it represented the initiate\'s journey from darkness to enlightenment. In this context, the cross was seen as a symbol of the spiritual path, with the horizontal axis representing the trials and challenges of the material world and the vertical axis representing the ascent of the soul to higher levels of consciousness.\n\nIn conclusion, the cross is a symbol with deep and multifaceted roots in human history, representing the sun, the intersection of the spiritual and material realms, and the path to enlightenment. Its association with Christianity has made it a potent and deeply meaningful symbol in the faith, representing salvation, redemption, and eternal life through faith in Christ.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [785, 5312, 374, 36948, 279, 1429, 65252, 323, 5089, 7735, 304, 31086, 11, 3637, 10746, 7988, 21261, 323, 33047, 5538, 38371, 367, 304, 50913, 323, 2477, 90205, 645, 3004, 25992, 13, 11445, 32372, 11, 4764, 11, 855, 1028, 31086, 323, 646, 387, 50300, 1182, 311, 13833, 85469, 323, 26735, 429, 1483, 432, 438, 264, 10381, 7735, 1293, 1573, 279, 7194, 315, 3686, 382, 19810, 1181, 27730, 13656, 19703, 11, 279, 5312, 702, 2525, 311, 387, 16510, 5815, 448, 279, 14788, 96322, 290, 315, 10588, 3686, 11, 879, 8469, 389, 264, 22360, 5312, 311, 518, 603, 369, 279, 39344, 315, 21941, 13, 1096, 15010, 702, 72254, 3260, 279, 5312, 448, 5538, 7290, 304, 31086, 11, 7735, 4849, 44935, 11, 55652, 11, 323, 34725, 2272, 1526, 9881, 304, 3686, 382, 1918, 882, 11, 279, 5312, 702, 4429, 389, 2155, 7586, 323, 49700, 2878, 31086, 11, 2670, 279, 