INFO 03-13 07:53:45 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-fa8664723d604f43866b82d6d5a8e738-0: prompt: "Populating the database with sample data is an important step in setting up the database for your web-based commercial appraisal report writing application. Here are some steps you can follow to populate the database with sample data in a MySQL database:\n\n1. Connect to the database: Connect to the database using a MySQL client tool such as the MySQL command-line client or a graphical user interface (GUI) tool such as phpMyAdmin.\n2. Insert sample data into the properties table: Insert sample data into the properties table using the following SQL command:\n\nINSERT INTO properties (location, size, age, condition)\nVALUES ('New York', 1000, 5, 'Good'),\n('Los Angeles', 2000, 10, 'Excellent'),\n('Chicago', 1500, 8, 'Fair');\n3. Insert sample data into the appraisal reports table: Insert sample data into the appraisal reports table using the following SQL command:\n\nINSERT INTO appraisal\\_reports (property\\_id, report\\_date, report\\_type, report\\_value)\nVALUES (1, '2022-01-01', 'Market Value', 1000000),\n(2, '2022-02-01', 'Market Value', 2000000),\n(3, '2022-03-01', 'Market Value', 1500000);\n4. Insert sample data into the users table: Insert sample data into the users table using the following SQL command:\n\nINSERT INTO users (username, email, password)\nVALUES ('john', '[john@example.com](mailto:john@example.com)', 'password1'),\n('jane', '[jane@example.com](mailto:jane@example.com)', 'password2'),\n('jim', '[jim@example.com](mailto:jim@example.com)', 'password3');\n\nBy following these steps, you can populate the database with sample data in a MySQL database for your web-based commercial appraisal report writing application. If you need further assistance, please let me know.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[]