INFO 03-13 07:53:46 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-4ef538e9d9b7489cb27fa4de479fc5b8-0: prompt: 'Certainly! I\'ll add the requested information as a supplement to Chapter c, Taxonomy Object Type.\n\nv. Using `get_the_terms()` to Retrieve Taxonomy Terms Linked to a Post\n\nThe `get_the_terms()` function can be used to obtain the taxonomy terms associated with a specific post. Here\'s an example of how to use `get_the_terms()` to retrieve the "Genre" taxonomy terms linked to a "Movie" post:\n```php\n// Retrieving \'Genre\' taxonomy terms for a specific \'Movie\' post\n$genres = get_the_terms($post_id, \'genre\');\n\nif ($genres && !is_wp_error($genres)) {\n    echo \'Genres: \';\n    $genre_list = array();\n\n    foreach ($genres as $genre) {\n        $genre_list[] = $genre->name;\n    }\n\n    echo implode(\', \', $genre_list);\n}\n```\nvi. Using `get_terms()` to Retrieve Terms from a Taxonomy\n\nThe `get_terms()` function allows you to retrieve all terms from a specific taxonomy. Here\'s an example of using `get_terms()` to obtain all terms from the "Genre" taxonomy:\n```php\n// Retrieving all terms from the \'Genre\' taxonomy\n$genres = get_terms(array(\n    \'taxonomy\' => \'genre\',\n    \'hide_empty\' => false,\n));\n\nif ($genres && !is_wp_error($genres)) {\n    foreach ($genres as $genre) {\n        echo $genre->name . \'<br>\';\n    }\n}\n```\nvii. Using `get_term()` and Term Metadata\n\nThe `get_term()` function can be used to obtain information about a specific term within a taxonomy. Here\'s an example of using `get_term()` to retrieve information about a "Genre" term and its associated metadata:\n```php\n// Retrieving a specific term from the \'Genre\' taxonomy\n$term_id = 5; // Replace with the actual term ID\n$genre = get_term($term_id, \'genre\');\n\nif ($genre && !is_wp_error($genre)) {\n    echo \'Name: \' . $genre->name . \'<br>\';\n    echo \'Description: \' . $genre->description . \'<br>\';\n\n    // Retrieving term metadata\n    $genre_icon = get_term_meta($term_id, \'genre_icon\', true);\n    echo \'Icon: \' . $genre_icon . \'<br>\';\n}\n```\nWith these additions, novice WordPress developers will have a deeper understanding of how to work with taxonomies, retrieve taxonomy terms, and utilize term metadata to create more dynamic and organized content on their websites.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [95456, 0, 358, 3278, 912, 279, 11223, 1995, 438, 264, 22047, 311, 15585, 272, 11, 15190, 16974, 3002, 3990, 382, 85, 13, 12091, 1565, 455, 16068, 37498, 54258, 311, 31562, 15190, 16974, 19591, 13114, 311, 264, 3877, 271, 785, 1565, 455, 16068, 37498, 54258, 729, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 6851, 279, 71806, 3793, 5815, 448, 264, 3151, 1736, 13, 5692, 594, 458, 3110, 315, 1246, 311, 990, 1565, 455, 16068, 37498, 54258, 311, 17179, 279, 330, 37525, 1, 71806, 3793, 10592, 311, 264, 330, 19668, 1, 1736, 510, 73594, 1208, 198, 322, 19470, 4405, 364, 37525, 6, 71806, 3793, 369, 264, 3151, 364, 19668, 6, 1736, 198, 3, 63911, 284, 633, 16068, 37498, 699, 2203, 842, 11, 364, 33613, 3755, 333, 1711, 63911, 1009, 753, 285, 39287, 4096, 699, 63911, 593, 341, 262, 1687, 364, 87828, 25, 19901, 262, 400, 33613, 2019, 284, 1334, 1428, 262, 4043, 1711, 63911, 438, 400, 33613, 8, 341, 286, 400, 33613, 2019, 1294, 284, 400, 33613, 405, 606, 280, 262, 555, 262, 1687, 26661, 13749, 6614, 400, 33613, 2019, 317, 532, 13874, 3989, 9971, 13, 12091, 1565, 455, 37498, 54258, 311, 31562, 19591, 504, 264, 15190, 16974, 271, 785, 1565, 455, 37498, 54258, 729, 6147, 498, 311, 17179, 678, 3793, 504, 264, 3151, 71806, 13, 5692, 594, 4