or episodic storylines, we can explore themes such as punishment and forgiveness, modernity, struggle with authority, class awareness, and authenticity. Here are a few potential storylines that incorporate these themes:\n* A vengeful ghost seeks retribution for a past injustice, forcing the group to confront themes of punishment and forgiveness.\n* The facility\'s new management implements advanced surveillance technology, creating an atmosphere of control and distrust that the teens must navigate.\n* A series of mysterious events at Los Padrinos reveals a hidden connection to a powerful figure in the community, highlighting themes of class and authority.\n* The group uncovers evidence of a decades-old cover-up involving the facility\'s dark past, questioning the authenticity of the new management\'s progressive image.\n\nTo balance the larger narrative arc with episodic storylines, we can use a structure similar to shows like "X-Files" and "Supernatural." Each episode will feature a self-contained mystery, while also dropping hints and clues that connect to the overarching story of the Devil\'s Den and Alex\'s sister\'s disappearance. This format will allow us to explore various themes and develop the characters while keeping the audience engaged with a mix of standalone and serialized storytelling.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any additional thoughts or ideas based on these suggestions, and we can continue refining the story together.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [13060, 498, 369, 697, 11682, 14507, 13, 20205, 389, 697, 11253, 11, 358, 614, 1045