amiliarizing yourself with the course structure and content.\n\t+ Spend the next 20 minutes watching Sections 1-2 of the course to learn the basics of DynamoDB, including how to create tables, work with data types, and use the AWS console and CLI.\n\t+ Spend the remaining 20 minutes watching Section 3 of the course to learn advanced topics such as partition keys, secondary indexes, and query optimization.\n\t+ Take a 10-minute break before moving on to the next session.\n\n1:00 PM - 1:50 PM (50 mins): AWS Services for Backend Development\n\n* Resource:\n\t+ "AWS Backend Services Overview" on AWS website (Documentation)\n* Time vs. Resources:\n\t+ Spend the first 10 minutes reading the documentation introduction and familiarizing yourself with the AWS backend services covered in this resource, including AWS Lambda, Amazon SNS, Amazon SQS, and AWS AppSync.\n\t+ Spend the next 20 minutes reading about AWS Lambda and how to use it to run code in response to events.\n\t+ Spend the next 10 minutes reading about Amazon SNS and Amazon SQS and how to use them for messaging and notifications.\n\t+ Spend the remaining 10 minutes reading about AWS AppSync and how to use it to build GraphQL APIs.\n\t+ Take a 10-minute break before wrapping up for the day.\n\nOverall, this study plan covers a wide range of topics related to building a backend using NodeJS, TypeScript, GraphQL, and AWS services. By the end of Day 1, you should have a solid understanding of the basics of', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 0, 5692, 594, 279, 6059, 220, 16, 3920, 3119, 448, 11682, 882