INFO 03-13 07:53:54 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-7131d15388744a21bd7914de947c0720-0: prompt: 'Yes, I can reproduce the table at the end of "Restricting TikTok (Part II)":\n\n| Bill | Key Provisions |\n| --- | --- |\n| No TikTok on Government Devices Act | Modifies an existing IEEPA exception allowing certain social media applications, including TikTok, to be used on government-issued devices by removing TikTok from the exception. |\n| National Security and Personal Data Protection Act | Removes an existing IEEPA exception that permits US companies to transfer personal data to foreign entities under certain circumstances, and requires a national security review for any such transfer. |\n| Protecting America\'s Data From Foreign Companies Act | Requires foreign companies to undergo a national security review before acquiring a US company with access to sensitive personal data. |\n| Social Media Privacy Protection and Consumer Rights Act | Requires social media companies to obtain user consent before sharing their personal data with third parties, and establishes a new federal agency to enforce privacy rules. |\n| American Privacy Protection Act | Establishes a comprehensive federal framework for protecting personal data and privacy, including requirements for companies to obtain user consent and disclose their data practices. |\n| National Security and Personal Data Protection Act | Removes an existing IEEPA exception that permits US companies to transfer personal data to foreign entities under certain circumstances, and requires a national security review for any such transfer. |\n\nThis table summarizes some of the key provisions of several bills that have been proposed in the US Congress to address the national security concerns raised by TikTok and other foreign-controlled apps. The provisions include modifications to existing IEEPA exceptions, requirements for national security reviews of data transfers, and the establishment of new federal agencies to enforce privacy rules and protect personal data.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [9454, 11, 358, 646, 22800, 279, 1965, 518, 279, 835, 315, 330, 50360, 849, 287, 72742, 52854, 320, 5800, 7946, 8, 51418, 91, 8596, 760, 5309, 1298, 40015, 9248, 91, 12448, 760, 12448, 9248, 91, 2308, 72742, 52854, 389, 10212, 40377, 3218, 760, 5650, 9606, 458, 6350, 358, 7099, 8041, 4683, 10693, 3654, 3590, 3687, 8357, 11, 2670, 72742, 52854, 11, 311, 387, 1483, 389, 3033, 12, 58226, 7611, 553, 17592, 72742, 52854, 504, 279, 4683, 13, 9248, 91, 5055, 8234, 323, 19207, 2885, 19171, 3218, 760, 38775, 458, 6350, 358, 7099, 8041, 4683, 429, 28690, 2274, 5110, 311, 8317, 4345, 821, 311, 7214, 14744, 1212, 3654, 13161, 11, 323, 7460, 264, 5313, 4763, 3395, 369, 894, 1741, 8317, 13, 9248, 91, 33663, 287, 5159, 594, 2885, 5542, 19078, 31786, 3218, 760, 44089, 7214, 5110, 311, 36671, 264, 5313, 4763, 3395, 1573, 41890, 264, 2274, 2813, 448, 2615, 311, 16216, 4345, 821, 13, 9248, 91, 9784, 7816, 18874, 19171, 323, 25197, 10512, 3218, 760, 44089, 3590, 3687, 5110, 311, 6851, 1196, 14433, 1573, 11560, 862, 4345, 821, 448, 4843, 9677, 11, 323, 63564, 264, 501, 6775, 9088, 311, 28162, 12345, 5601, 13, 9248, 91, 3693, 18874, 19171, 3218, 760, 39398, 288, 264, 15817, 6775, 12626, 369, 22184, 4345, 821, 323, 12345, 11, 2670, 8502, 369, 5110, 311, 6851, 1196, 14433, 323, 35233, 862, 821, 12378, 13, 9248, 91, 5055, 8234, 323, 19207, 2885, 19171, 3218, 760, 38775, 458, 6350, 358, 7099, 8041, 4683, 429, 28690, 2274, 5110, 311, 8317, 4345, 821, 311, 7214, 14744, 1212, 3654, 13161, 11, 323, 7460, 264