INFO 03-13 07:53:55 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-bb7f26122d4945149e958534d76c6931-0: prompt: "Adding a simple AI is not too difficult and should be manageable with the current code. We can create a basic AI that follows a strategy in the following order:\n\n1. If there's a winning move, take it.\n2. If the opponent has a winning move, block it.\n3. If neither of the above, make a random move.\n\nHere's the implementation of the AI:\n```c\nVector2 AIGetMove() {\n    Vector2 bestMove = {-1, -1};\n    Cell tempBoard[BOARD_SIZE][BOARD_SIZE];\n\n    // Copy the current board state\n    memcpy(tempBoard, board, BOARD_SIZE * BOARD_SIZE * sizeof(Cell));\n\n    // Check for a winning move\n    for (int i = 0; i < BOARD_SIZE; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < BOARD_SIZE; j++) {\n            if (tempBoard[i][j] == EMPTY) {\n                tempBoard[i][j] = PLAYER2;\n                if (GetWinningDirection(PLAYER2)) {\n                    return (Vector2){j, i};\n                }\n                tempBoard[i][j] = EMPTY;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Check for the opponent's winning move and block it\n    for (int i = 0; i < BOARD_SIZE; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < BOARD_SIZE; j++) {\n            if (tempBoard[i][j] == EMPTY) {\n                tempBoard[i][j] = PLAYER1;\n                if (GetWinningDirection(PLAYER1)) {\n                    return (Vector2){j, i};\n                }\n                tempBoard[i][j] = EMPTY;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // If neither of the above, make a random move\n    Vector2 moves[BOARD_SIZE * BOARD_SIZE];\n    int moveCount = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < BOARD_SIZE; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < BOARD_SIZE; j++) {\n            if (board[i][j] == EMPTY) {\n                moves[moveCount++] = (Vector2){j, i};\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (moveCount > 0) {\n        bestMove = moves[GetRandomValue(0, moveCount - 1)];\n    }\n\n    return bestMove;\n}\n```\nAdd this `AIGetMove` function to your code, and then update the `main` function to call it when it's Player 2's turn. Here's an example of how to modify the `main` function:\n```c\nif (!gameOver) {\n    Vector2 move;\n    if (currentPlayer == PLAYER1 && IsMouseButtonPressed(MOUSE_LEFT_BUTTON)) {\n        move = GetMouseCell();\n        if (board[(int)move.x][(int)move.y] == EMPTY) {\n            board[(int)move.x][(int)move.y] = currentPlayer;\n            currentPlayer = PLAYER2;\n        }\n    } else if (currentPlayer == PLAYER2) {\n        move = AIGetMove();\n        if (board[(int)move.x][(int)move.y] == EMPTY) {\n            board[(int)move.x][(int)move.y] = currentPlayer;\n            currentPlayer = PLAYER1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // ... (rest of the code)\n}\n```\nThis implementation should add a simple AI to your Tic Tac Toe game. The AI will first attempt to win, then block the opponent's win, and finally make a random move if neither of the previous conditions are met.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [32308, 264, 4285, 15235, 374, 537, 2238, 5000, 323, 1265, 387, 70028, 448, 279, 1482, 2038, 13, 1205, 646, 1855, 264, 6770, 15235, 429, 11017, 264, 8282, 304, 279, 2701, 1973, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 1052, 594, 264, 10987, 3271, 11, 1896, 432, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 14704, 702, 264, 10987, 3271, 11, 2504, 432, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 13866, 315, 279, 3403, 11, 1281, 264, 4194, 3271, 382, 8420, 594, 279, 8129, 315, 279, 15235, 510, 73594, 66, 198, 3781, 17, 362, 1914, 295, 9860, 368, 341, 262, 4196, 17, 1850, 9860, 284, 29669, 16, 11, 481, 16, 2440, 262, 13972, 2730, 11932,