INFO 03-13 07:53:58 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-6ab05c4ca60c43b596e683ca6667adc4-0: prompt: 'I apologize for the confusion. You are correct, the `world_size` argument is missing in the `Trainer` class initialization. It should be added as an additional argument, like so:\n```python\nclass Trainer:\n    def __init__(self, train_csv_path, val_csv_path, tokenizer, max_len, batch_size, num_workers, device, rank, world_size):\n        self.train_csv_path = train_csv_path\n        self.val_csv_path = val_csv_path\n        self.tokenizer = tokenizer\n        self.max_len = max_len\n        self.batch_size = batch_size\n        self.num_workers = num_workers\n        self.device = device\n        self.rank = rank\n        self.world_size = world_size\n        \n        self.train_loader, self.val_loader = get_data_loaders(train_csv_path, val_csv_path, tokenizer, max_len, batch_size, num_workers, rank, world_size)\n        \n        self.model = BertClassifier(num_classes=8).to(device)\n        self.criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n        self.optimizer = AdamW(self.model.parameters(), lr=2e-5, correct_bias=False)\n        self.scheduler = get_linear_schedule_with_warmup(self.optimizer, num_warmup_steps=0, num_training_steps=len(self.train_loader)*10)\n        \n        if torch.cuda.device_count() > 1:\n            self.model = nn.DataParallel(self.model)\n        \n        self.distributed = False\n        if torch.cuda.device_count() > 1:\n            self.distributed = True\n            torch.distributed.init_process_group(backend="nccl", rank=self.rank, world_size=self.world_size)\n            self.model = nn.parallel.DistributedDataParallel(self.model)\n```\nAnd when you initialize the `Trainer` class, you should provide the `world_size` argument as well:\n```python\ntrainer = Trainer(train_csv_path, val_csv_path, tokenizer, max_len, batch_size, num_workers, device, rank, world_size)\n```', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=