INFO 03-13 07:53:58 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-494c81c05cb84fe79f03cb338e09c77b-0: prompt: 'Here\'s an example code for adding remote agents (such as forest guards and police officers) to the control center with encryption using MQTT protocol:\n```python\nimport paho.mqtt.client as mqtt\nimport ssl\nimport json\n\n# define MQTT broker settings\nMQTT_BROKER = "mqtt.example.com"\nMQTT_PORT = 8883\nMQTT_USERNAME = "username"\nMQTT_PASSWORD = "password"\nMQTT_CLIENT_ID = "client_id"\nMQTT_TOPIC = "topic/#"\n\n# define SSL settings\nMQTT_CA_CERTS = "ca.crt"\nMQTT_CERTFILE = "client.crt"\nMQTT_KEYFILE = "client.key"\n\n# create MQTT client object\nclient = mqtt.Client(client_id=MQTT_CLIENT_ID)\n\n# set SSL context\ncontext = ssl.create_default_context()\ncontext.load_verify_locations(cafile=MQTT_CA_CERTS)\ncontext.load_cert_chain(certfile=MQTT_CERTFILE, keyfile=MQTT_KEYFILE)\n\n# connect to MQTT broker with SSL/TLS encryption\nclient.tls_set_context(context)\nclient.username_pw_set(username=MQTT_USERNAME, password=MQTT_PASSWORD)\nclient.connect(MQTT_BROKER, MQTT_PORT)\n\n# define remote agent data\nremote_agent = {\n    "id": "forest_guard_001",\n    "name": "John Doe",\n    "location": {\n        "lat": 39.9526,\n        "lng": -75.1652\n    }\n}\n\n# publish remote agent data to control center topic\nclient.publish("control_center/remote_agents", json.dumps(remote_agent))\n\n# subscribe to remote agent topic\nclient.subscribe("remote_agents/#")\n\n# define callback function for incoming messages\ndef on_message(client, userdata, message):\n    payload = message.payload.decode()\n    if message.topic.startswith("remote_agents/"):\n        remote_agent_data = json.loads(payload)\n        print("Received remote agent data:", remote_agent_data)\n\n# set callback function for incoming messages\nclient.on_message = on_message\n\n# start MQTT loop\nclient.loop_forever()\n```\nIn this example code, the MQTT protocol is used for communication between the remote agents (e.g. forest guards and police officers) and the control center. SSL/TLS encryption is used to secure the communication. The `paho.mqtt` Python library is used for MQTT communication.\n\nThe code defines the MQTT broker settings, SSL settings, and creates an MQTT client object. The `remote_agent` data is defined and published to the `control_center/remote_agents` topic. The code also subscribes to the `remote_agents/#` topic and defines a callback function for incoming messages. The `on_message` function is called when a new message is received, and it can handle different topics based on the message topic.\n\nThe code can be further extended to handle different types of data from the remote agents, such as sensor readings, images, or location data. The control center can use the received data to visualize the status of the remote agents on an interactive map and take appropriate actions based on the data.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [8420, 594, 458, 3110, 2038, 369, 7842, 8699, 13009, 320, 20805, 438, 13638, 26178, 323, 4282, 9611, 8, 311, 279, 2524, 4126, 448, 25463, 1667, 61424, 11507, 510, 73594, 12669, 198, 474, 281, 28582, 744, 32267, 6581, 438, 59431, 198, 474, 33537, 198, 474, 2951, 271, 2, 6979, 61424, 22316, 5003, 198, 35169, 14903, 1668, 1285, 79842, 284, 330, 86576, 7724, 905, 698, 35169, 14903, 12377, 284, 220, 23, 23, 23, 18, 198, 35169, 14903, 42696, 284, 330, 5113, 698, 35169, 14903, 23059, 284, 330, 3833, 698, 35169, 14903, 22521, 3450, 284, 330, 2972, 842, 698, 35169, 14903, 74077, 284, 330, 16411, 26559, 1837, 2, 6979, 25316, 5003, 1