INFO 03-13 07:54:00 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-1085bfdf18d04796a28b8d3255dd0fe8-0: prompt: 'Boosting is a type of ensemble method in machine learning that combines several weak models to produce a single strong model. Unlike bagging, which trains multiple base models independently, boosting trains the base models sequentially, each time correcting the mistakes of the previous model.\n\nThe basic idea behind boosting is to train a weak model on the data, and then use the errors made by this model to train the next model. This process is repeated multiple times, each time with the errors made by the previous model used to train the next model. The final prediction is then made by combining the predictions of all the individual models.\n\nIn general, boosting algorithms work by assigning a weight to each instance in the training data, with instances that were misclassified by previous models given a higher weight. This way, the next model will focus more on the instances that were misclassified, and less on the instances that were correctly classified.\n\nBoosting has been shown to be effective in a variety of applications, particularly in the context of classification problems. Some popular boosting algorithms include AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [52363, 287, 374, 264, 943, 315, 39026, 1714, 304, 5662, 6832, 429, 32411, 3807, 7469, 4119, 311, 8193, 264, 3175, 3746, 1614, 13, 26048, 8968, 3173, 11, 892, 27688, 5248, 2331, 4119, 28135, 11, 54928, 27688, 279, 2331, 4119, 94559, 11, 1817, 882, 81375, 279, 20