INFO 03-13 07:54:01 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-af8c964f36f24f5db4159840d5282962-0: prompt: "Understanding Cross Workspace Collaboration Feature\n\nCross Workspace Collaboration (XWC) is a new feature that allows different workspaces, even those with the same domain, to collaborate with each other. This can be particularly useful for companies with multiple departments or subsidiaries that want to maintain separate workspaces while still being able to communicate and work together. To use XWC, at least one of the workspaces needs to be on a pro or higher plan. The paid workspace can then invite other workspaces to collaborate, regardless of whether they belong to the same company or not.\n\nKey Differences Between Guest User and Cross Workspace Collaboration Features\n\n1. Domain requirements: Guest users must have a domain external to the account, whereas with XWC, workspaces with the same domain can collaborate.\n2. Gaming the system: With XWC, it's possible for users to game the system by having multiple workspaces with a limited number of users in each, using only one paid workspace to collaborate with the others. However, this behavior will be monitored and controlled on a case-by-case basis.\n3. Expansion possibilities: XWC opens up the opportunity for expansion by allowing a paid workspace for one department to collaborate with other departments that are using a separate, free workspace.\n\nQnA:\n\nQ: Can the same domain be used for Cross Workspace Collaboration?\nA: Yes, workspaces with the same domain can collaborate with each other using Cross Workspace Collaboration.\n\nQ: Is it possible for users to game the system with Cross Workspace Collaboration?\nA: Yes, it is possible for users to game the system by having multiple workspaces with a limited number of users in each and using only one paid workspace to collaborate with the others. However, this behavior will be monitored and controlled on a case-by-case basis.\n\nQ: How can Cross Workspace Collaboration be used as an expansion play?\nA: Cross Workspace Collaboration can be leveraged for expansion by allowing a paid workspace for one department to collaborate with other departments that are using a separate, free workspace. This allows for more efficient collaboration without the need for all departments to pay for additional users.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [70151, 11261, 70934, 86587, 19998, 271, 28501, 70934, 86587, 320, 55, 25459, 8, 374, 264, 501, 4565, 429, 6147, 2155, 975, 44285, 11, 1496, 1846, 448, 279, 1852, 7947, 11, 311, 50596, 448, 1817, 1008, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 7945, 5390, 369, 5110, 448, 5248, 25215, 476, 71102, 429, 1366, 311, 10306, 8651, 975, 44285, 1393, 2058, 1660, 2952, 311, 19032, 323, 975, 3786, 13, 2014, 990, 1599, 25459, 11, 518, 3245, 825, 315, 279, 975, 44285, 3880, 311, 387, 389, 264, 462, 476, 5080, 3119, 13, 576, 7171, 27514, 646, 1221, 21399, 1008, 975, 44285, 311, 50596, 11, 15484, 315, 3425, 807, 9173, 311, 279, 1852, 2813, 476, 537, 382, 1592, 85797, 27133, 26215, 2657, 323, 11261, 70934, 86587, 19710, 271, 16, 13, 21070, 8502, 25, 26215, 3847, 1969, 614, 264, 7947, 9250, 311, 279, 2692, 11, 19853, 448, 1599, 25459, 11, 975, 44285, 448, 279, 1852, 7947, 646, 50596, 624, 17, 13, 30462, 279, 1849, 25, 3085, 1599, 25459, 11, 432, 594, 3204, 369, 3847, 311, 1809, 279, 1849, 553, 3432, 5248, 975, 44285, 448, 264, 7199, 1372, 315, 3847, 304, 1817, 11, 1667, 1172, 825, 7171, 27514, 311, 50596, 448, 279, 3800, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 7709, 686, 387, 40123, 323, 14071, 389, 264, 1142, 14319, 38485, 8037, 624, 18, 13,