INFO 03-13 07:54:01 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-99b5ce7f9558486fb3c483c2cb945607-0: prompt: 'You are correct, my apologies for the oversight. Since the `borderWidth` parameter is a double and cannot be null, it will throw an error if the border is not set on a particular side.\n\nTo avoid this, you can create a new class `BorderSideEx` which extends `BorderSide` and can take an optional width and color.\n```\nclass BorderSideEx extends BorderSide {\n  BorderSideEx({double width, Color color})\n      : super(width: width, color: color);\n}\n```\nAnd then use it in the RoundedCornerWidget,\n```\nclass RoundedCornerWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  final double radius;\n  final BorderSideEx top;\n  final BorderSideEx right;\n  final BorderSideEx bottom;\n  final BorderSideEx left;\n  final bool topLeft;\n  final bool topRight;\n  final bool bottomLeft;\n  final bool bottomRight;\n  final Widget child;\n\n  RoundedCornerWidget({\n    this.radius = 10,\n    this.top = const BorderSideEx(),\n    this.right = const BorderSideEx(),\n    this.bottom = const BorderSideEx(),\n    this.left = const BorderSideEx(),\n    this.topLeft = true,\n    this.topRight = true,\n    this.bottomLeft = true,\n    this.bottomRight = true,\n    @required this.child,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    var borderRadius = BorderRadius.only(\n      topLeft: topLeft ? Radius.circular(radius) : Radius.zero,\n      topRight: topRight ? Radius.circular(radius) : Radius.zero,\n      bottomLeft: bottomLeft ? Radius.circular(radius) : Radius.zero,\n      bottomRight: bottomRight ? Radius.circular(radius) : Radius.zero,\n    );\n\n    return Container(\n      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n        borderRadius: borderRadius,\n        border: Border(\n          top: top,\n          right: right,\n          bottom: bottom,\n          left: left\n        ),\n      ),\n      child: child,\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\nYou can use this widget like this:\n```\nRoundedCornerWidget(\n  topLeft: true,\n  topRight: false,\n  bottomLeft: false,\n  bottomRight: false,\n  top: BorderSideEx(width: 2, color: Colors.green),\n  left: BorderSideEx(width: 2, color: Colors.green),\n  child: Container(\n    color: Colors.blue,\n    width: 100,\n    height: 100,\n  ),\n),\n```\nThis way, you can pass `null` or not passing any value to the border side property, which means no border.\n\nPlease let me know if this solution works for you or if you have any further question.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2610, 525, 4396, 11, 847, 72173, 369, 279, 37089, 13, 8704, 279, 1565, 9461, 3327, 63, 5733, 374, 264, 1990, 323, 4157, 387, 845, 11, 432, 686, 2510, 458, 1465, 421, 279, 3886, 374, 537, 738, 389, 264, 3953, 3108, 382, 1249, 5648, 419, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 501, 536, 1565, 10691, 16384, 840, 63, 892, 2239, 1565, 10691, 16384, 63, 323, 646, 1896, 458, 10101, 2374, 323, 1894, 624, 13874, 3989, 1040, 72401, 840, 2239, 72401, 341, 220, 72401, 840, 2306, 4331, 2374, 11, 3478, 1894, 3518, 414, 549, 2256, 16425, 25, 2374, 11, 1894, 25, 1894, 317, 532, 13874, 3989, 3036, 1221, 990, 432, 304, 279, 57450, 50352, 4548, 345, 13874, 3989, 1040, 57450, 50352, 4548, 2239, 36798, 341, 220, 1590, 1990, 10578, 280, 220, 1590, 72401, 840, 1909, 280, 220, 1590, 72401, 840, 1290, 280, 220, 1590, 72401, 840, 5622, 280, 220, 1590, 72401, 840, 2115, 280, 220, 1590, 1807, 79103, 280, 220, 1590, 1807, 1909, 5979, 280, 220, 1590, 1807, 5622, 5415, 280, 220, 1590, 1807, 5622, 5979, 280, 220, 1590, 12980, 1682, 401, 220, 57450, 50352, 4548, 2262, 262, 419, 34094, 284, 220,