INFO 03-13 07:54:04 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-743ac6fc126a4192a84b9ce92712bc4a-0: prompt: 'Sure, here are the translations of the 10 verses from "Ulladu Narpadu" which mention the Heart Center:\n\n1. "If one investigates the nature of the mind, one will find it to be nothing other than the power of the Self. Therefore, by any means whatsoever, it is necessary to still the mind. The only way to do this is to inquire \'Who am I?\' by turning one\'s mind inwards, with one-pointedness, towards the Heart."\n2. "If the ego rises, all else will also rise; if it subsides, all else will also subside. The ego is therefore the cause of all one\'s bondage and suffering. Inquire within yourself as to what this ego is, and you will find that it is nothing other than a bundle of thoughts and concepts centered around the \'I\' thought. The ego has no real existence apart from these thoughts."\n3. "The Heart is the hub of all spiritual practice. As one repeatedly practices turning the mind inward and focusing it on the Heart, one develops the ability to stay there. Eventually, the Heart will reveal its true nature as the Self."\n4. "The Heart is the seat of consciousness, and the source of all thoughts and actions. One who is established in the Heart sees everything as the Self and experiences unbroken peace and bliss. To attain this state, it is necessary to inquire \'Who am I?\' and to abide as the Self."\n5. "The Heart is the treasure-house of unending bliss, the source of all light and knowledge. It is the very embodiment of the Self. One who knows the Self as residing in the Heart is freed from all bondage and ignorance."\n6. "The Heart is not something to be gained anew. It is always present, shining forth as the pure consciousness within. It is simply a matter of removing the false identifications and concepts which veil it. Therefore, one should turn the mind inward and inquire \'Who am I?\' with earnestness and devotion."\n7. "The Heart is the abode of the Supreme Reality, which is eternal, infinite, and beyond all concepts and limitations. By focusing the mind on the Heart and inquiring \'Who am I?\', one can transcend all duality and experience the unchanging Reality."\n8. "The Heart is the source of all grace, love, and compassion. It is the very embodiment of the Divine. To turn the mind towards the Heart is to enter into the Divine Presence and to be enveloped by its boundless love and compassion."\n9. "The Heart is the gateway to the Supreme Reality. It is the point of convergence for all spiritual paths and practices. By inquiring', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 36693, 315, 279, 220, 16, 15, 49299, 504, 330, 52, 654, 329, 84, 451, 7876, 329, 84, 1, 892, 6286, 279, 17965, 5832, 1447, 16, 13, 330, 2679, 825, 83263, 279, 6993, 315, 279, 3971, 11, 825, 686, 1477, 432, 311, 387, 4302, 1008, 1091, 279, 2355, 315, 279, 10115, 13, 15277, 11, 553, 894, 3363, 35634, 11, 432, 374, 5871, 311, 2058, 279, 3971, 13, 576, 1172, 1616, 311, 653, 419, 374, 311, 67170, 364, 15191, 1079, 358, 20224, 553, 13054, 825, 594, 3971, 304, 4014, 11, 448, 825, 16574, 291, 2090, 11, 6974, 279, 17965, 10040, 17, 13, 330, 2679, 279, 36274, 37168, 11, 678, 770, 686, 1083, 10000, 26, 421, 432, 5147, 3341, 11, 678, 770, 686, 1083, 1186, 2929, 13, 576, 36274, 374, 8916, 279, 5240, 315, 678, 825, 594, 42494, 323, 15691, 13, 758, 984, 2878, 6133, 438, 311, 1128, 419, 36274, 374, 11, 323, 498, 686, 1477, 429, 432, 374, 4302, 1008, 1091, 264, 12894, 315, 11303, 323, 18940, 30188, 2163, 279, 364, 40, 6, 3381, 13, 576, 36