INFO 03-13 07:54:04 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-7e53ffea885a41e5ae464aa270740c62-0: prompt: 'Sure, I can help you modify the `CachedFeed` class to have the same interface as other feeds, including the ability to make recommendations and to check if a user can select items from the feed.\n\nHere\'s an updated implementation for the `CachedFeed` class:\n```ruby\nclass CachedFeed\n  def initialize(user, feed_cache, feed_generator)\n    @user = user\n    @feed_cache = feed_cache\n    @feed_generator = feed_generator\n  end\n\n  def get_feed\n    feed_name = "user_#{@user.id}_feed"\n    @feed_cache.get(feed_name) { @feed_generator.call(@user) }\n  end\n\n  def invalidate_feed\n    feed_name = "user_#{@user.id}_feed"\n    @feed_cache.invalidate(feed_name)\n  end\n\n  # Make recommendations for the user based on the cached feed\n  def make_recommendations\n    feed = get_feed\n    # Implement recommendation logic using the cached feed\n  end\n\n  # Check if the user can select items from the cached feed\n  def can_select?\n    feed = get_feed\n    # Implement selection logic using the cached feed\n  end\nend\n```\nThe `CachedFeed` class now includes two new methods, `make_recommendations` and `can_select?`, which allow it to have the same interface as other feeds.\n\nThe `make_recommendations` method generates recommendations for the user based on the cached feed. It first retrieves the cached feed using the `get_feed` method, and then implements the recommendation logic using the cached feed.\n\nThe `can_select?` method checks if the user is allowed to select items from the cached feed. It first retrieves the cached feed using the `get_feed` method, and then implements the selection logic using the cached feed.\n\nNote that the implementation of the recommendation and selection logic is not included in this example, since it depends on the specific requirements of your application. You would need to provide your own implementation of these methods based on your application requirements.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 358, 646, 1492, 498, 5602, 279, 1565, 70293, 28916, 63, 536, 311, 614, 279, 1852, 3749, 438, 1008, 34396, 11, 2670, 279, 5726, 311, 1281, 18564, 323, 311, 1779, 421, 264, 1196, 646, 3293, 3589, 504, 279, 5395, 382, 8420, 594, 458, 6049, 8129, 369, 279, 1565, 70293, 28916, 63, 536, 510, 73594, 46275, 198, 1040, 74205, 28916, 198, 220, 707, 9468, 4277, 11, 5395, 11529, 11, 5395, 25813, 340, 262, 569, 872, 284, 1196, 198, 262, 569, 11184, 11529, 284, 5395, 11529, 198, 262, 569, 11184, 25813, 284, 5395, 25813, 198, 220, 835, 271, 220, 707, 633, 42390, 198, 262, 5395, 1269, 284, 330, 872, 62, 84154, 872, 1764, 19444, 11184, 698, 262, 569, 11184, 11529, 670, 67886, 1269, 8, 314, 569, 11184, 25813, 8524, 5957, 872, 8, 456, 220, 835, 271, 220, 707, 39943, 42390, 198, 262, 5395, 1269, 284, 330, 872, 62, 84154, 872, 1764, 19444, 11184, 698, 262, 569, 11184, 11529, 75319, 67886, 1269, 340, 220, 835, 271, 220, 671, 7405, 18564, 369, 279, 1196, 3118, 389, 279, 20579, 5395, 198, 220, 707, 1281, 99084, 804, 198, 262, 5395, 284, 633, 42390, 198, 262, 671, 31075, 27682, 12218, 1667, 279, 20579, 5395, 198, 220, 835, 271, 220, 671, 4248, 421, 279, 1196, 646, 3293, 3589, 504, 279, 20579, 5395, 198, 220, 707, 646, 13051, 5267, 262, 5395, 284, 633, 42390, 198, 262, 671, 31075, 6589, 12218, 1667, 279, 20579, 5395, 198, 220, 835, 198, 408, 198, 13874, 3989, 785, 1565, 70293, 28916, 63, 536, 1431, 5646, 1378, 501, 5413, 11, 1565, 6927, 99084, 804, 63, 323, 1565, 4814, 13051, 30, 7808, 892, 2138, 432, 311, 614, 27