INFO 03-13 07:54:04 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-69b6c4855f974e01b8eaf3f1c34eab9a-0: prompt: 'For a $200 advertising budget, we\'ll focus on low-cost, high-impact marketing strategies to promote "Bouncy Hoops: The Magical Basketball Adventure." Here\'s a suggested advertising campaign:\n\n1. Social Media:\n\nCreate eye-catching visuals and engaging content to post on Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter. You can use free design tools like Canva to create images for your posts. Aim to post 3-4 times per week, with a mix of promotional content, fun facts about the story, and behind-the-scenes details.\n\n* Cost: Free (if you design the graphics yourself)\n1. Local Library or Bookstore Promotion:\n\nReach out to your local library or bookstore and inquire about opportunities for promoting your book. They might be willing to display your book or allow you to host a free reading event for kids.\n\n* Cost: Free (minus the cost of any promotional materials you provide, such as posters or bookmarks)\n1. Email Marketing:\n\nCreate an email list of friends, family, and other contacts who might be interested in the book. Send out a well-crafted email announcing the book\'s release, along with links to purchase the book and ways to spread the word.\n\n* Cost: Free (if you use your personal email or a free email marketing service like Mailchimp)\n1. Press Release:\n\nWrite a press release about the book and send it to local newspapers, blogs, and other media outlets. This could lead to free publicity in the form of articles or interviews. You can find free press release templates online to help you craft your message.\n\n* Cost: Free (if you write and distribute the press release yourself)\n1. Facebook Advertising:\n\nUse a portion of your budget to run a targeted Facebook ad campaign. You can create an ad with a captivating image and a strong call-to-action, and target users interested in children\'s books, basketball, and similar topics. Start with a small budget to test the effectiveness of your ad, and adjust your spending based on the results.\n\n* Cost: $50 (you can adjust the amount based on your desired reach and ad performance)\n1. Book Giveaway:\n\nHost a giveaway on social media or through your email list, offering a free copy of the book to one or more lucky winners. This will create buzz around the book and encourage people to share the giveaway with their friends and followers.\n\n* Cost: $20 (the cost of one or two copies of the book, plus shipping)\n1. Create a Book Trailer:\n\nCreate a short, engaging book trailer using free or low-cost video editing software, such as iMovie or Lightworks. Share the trailer on social media and include it in your email marketing efforts.\n\n* Cost: Free (if you create the trailer yourself using existing images and royalty-free music)\n\nTotal Advertising Budget: $70 (plus the cost of promotional materials and shipping for the giveaway). This leaves you with $130 to invest in additional promotional efforts or save for future marketing campaigns.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2461, 264, 400, 17, 15, 15, 12876, 8039, 11, 582, 3278, 5244, 389, 3347, 40138, 11, 1550, 12, 57300, 8493, 14830, 311, 11926, 330, 33, 81301, 17275, 3721, 25, 576, 72710, 46489, 32012, 1189, 5692, 594, 264, 11827, 12876, 4796, 1447, 16, 13, 9784, 7816, 1447, 4021, 7912, 83324, 52977, 323, 22570, 2213, 311, 1736, 389, 5573, 11, 13991, 11, 323, 6271, 13, 1446, 646, 990, 1910, 2884, 7375, 1075, 2980, 6586, 311, 1855, 5335, 369, 697, 7999, 13, 70615, 311, 1736, 220, 18, 12, 19, 3039, 817, 2003, 11, 448, 264,