INFO 03-13 07:54:04 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-e57a04131f9646229c7cbf1bf758b374-0: prompt: 'I apologize for the confusion. When I said "You can use each column as an input to your model, and train the model using those columns," I did not mean that you need to train 20 separate models. Instead, you can train a single model using all the columns in the dataframe as input features.\n\nIn other words, you can feed the entire dataframe (45000,20) as input to the model, and the model should be able to learn the relationship between the power consumption and each RPM.\n\nYou will need to treat your data as multivariate time-series data, which is a set of multiple correlated time series. This means that each RPM would be considered as an additional feature.\n\nTo achieve this, you can train the model with a 3D tensor with the shape of (samples, timesteps, features) where features are the number of RPMs. Since you have the data for 45000 timestamps, you can select some of them as timesteps and remaining as samples.\n\nIn this way, you\'ll train a single model that can make predictions for all the RPMs, based on the past observations, with the ability to generalize well and predict the power consumption for any RPM.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions or need more help.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [40, 36879, 369, 279, 21340, 13, 3197, 358, 1053, 330, 2610, 646, 990, 1817, 3250, 438, 458, 1946, 311, 697, 1614, 11, 323, 5426, 279, 1614, 1667, 1846, 8147, 1335, 358, 1521, 537, 3076, 429, 498, 1184, 311, 5426, 220, 17, 15, 8651, 4119, 1