INFO 03-13 07:54:05 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-a14f91b99d1849feb152063938a8ea0e-0: prompt: 'Sure, you can modify the regular expression to match either the full file path or a partial file path by using a non-capturing group with an optional forward slash before the first capturing group like this:\n```regex\n/(?:(?<=\\/)|^)(?<pn>\\d{4,9})\\/(?<type>LA|LSt|LS|SV)_(?<year>\\d{4})(_(?<month>\\d{2}))?_(?<pn2>\\d{4,9})(_(?<version>\\d{2}))?.pdf$/\n```\nThis modified regular expression includes a non-capturing group `(?:...)` with a positive lookbehind `(?<=...)` for a forward slash (`/`) followed by the start of the string anchor `^`. This allows the regular expression to match the first capturing group whether it is preceded by a forward slash or not.\n\nHere is a breakdown of the modified regular expression:\n\n* `/(?:(?<=\\/)|^)` - Non-capturing group with a positive lookbehind for a forward slash or start of string anchor\n* `(?<pn>\\d{4,9})\\/` - First capturing group for a sequence of 4 to 9 digits followed by a forward slash\n* `(?<type>LA|LSt|LS|SV)` - Second capturing group for the allowed values LA, LSt, LS, or SV\n* `_(?<year>\\d{4})` - Third capturing group for a sequence of 4 digits following an underscore\n* `(_(?<month>\\d{2}))?` - Optional fourth capturing group for a sequence of 2 digits following an underscore, preceded by another underscore\n* `_(?<pn2>\\d{4,9})` - Fifth capturing group for a sequence of 4 to 9 digits following an underscore\n* `(_(?<version>\\d{2}))?` - Optional sixth capturing group for a sequence of 2 digits following an underscore, preceded by another underscore\n* `\\.pdf$/` - Required suffix for a file extension of .pdf at the end of the string\n\nThis modified regular expression should match both full file paths and partial file paths that include the first capturing group with a sequence of 4 to 9 digits followed by a forward slash. I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or concerns.', params