INFO 03-13 07:54:06 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-48b7c7fb2266454186a04804f7c38844-0: prompt: 'Project Title: Advancing Jayhawks Rising: A Data-Driven Approach to Achieving Institutional Priorities\n\nProject Synopsis:\n\nThe University of Kansas has outlined a comprehensive plan called "Jayhawks Rising," which focuses on three mission-based institutional priorities: Student Success, Healthy and Vibrant Communities, and Research and Discovery. To successfully execute these objectives, a collaborative four-year project will leverage the expertise of four key participants: Jason Koepp, Sean Steinle, Leigh Sands, and Thomas Skinner. This project will employ their unique skill sets in data collection, analysis, survey design, and project management to inform and drive decision-making for each of the 13 objectives.\n\nYear 1: Data Collection and Benchmarking\n\n* Jason will create and administer surveys and web intercepts through Qualtrics to gather experiential data (xdata) from university employees and students, focusing on key indicators of success for each objective.\n* Sean will analyze operational data (odata) using SAS coding and Oracle Analytics Cloud to establish baseline metrics for each objective and identify areas requiring improvement.\n* Leigh, as the project manager, will coordinate communication between the team members and ensure timely completion of tasks.\n* Thomas will advise on survey design to maximize data quality and minimize respondent burden.\n\nYear 2: Data Analysis and Strategy Development\n\n* Jason and Leigh will work together to analyze the xdata collected, identifying trends and areas of concern.\n* Sean will perform in-depth analysis of odata to discover patterns, correlations, and potential causal factors for the identified issues.\n* Thomas will provide insights and recommendations for improving survey methodologies and data collection strategies.\n* The team will develop data-driven strategies and action plans to address the identified issues, focusing on the most impactful interventions for each objective.\n\nYear 3: Implementation and Monitoring\n\n* The team will collaborate with university stakeholders to implement the developed strategies and action plans.\n* Jason and Leigh will continue to administer and manage surveys, incorporating adjustments based on Thomas\'s recommendations, and monitor xdata to measure the effectiveness of interventions.\n* Sean will monitor odata to evaluate progress toward achieving the objectives and identify any new or emerging issues.\n\nYear 4: Evaluation and Reporting\n\n* The team will conduct a comprehensive evaluation of the project\'s impact on the 13 objectives, drawing on both xdata and odata.\n* Sean will perform a final analysis to assess the extent to which the objectives have been met and identify any remaining challenges.\n* The team will develop a final report outlining the project\'s successes, challenges, and recommendations for future initiatives.\n* Leigh, as project manager, will ensure the timely completion of the final report and its dissemination to university stakeholders and decision-makers.\n\nThis four-year project will enable the University of Kansas to effectively execute the Jayhawks Rising plan by utilizing the specialized skills of four active participants in the fields of data collection, analysis, and survey design. The project\'s data-driven approach will ensure that the university makes informed decisions and takes strategic actions to achieve its mission-based institutional priorities.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_to