INFO 03-13 07:54:08 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-8dc0b69721394bc6aebaa974813f5898-0: prompt: 'Sure! Here is a comprehensive list of use cases for an online booking system that covers various aspects of the system:\n\n1. Search Resources: As a customer, I want to be able to search for available resources (such as conference rooms, equipment, or vehicles) based on various criteria (such as location, capacity, and type) so that I can find the resources that meet my needs.\n2. View Resource Details: As a customer, I want to be able to view detailed information about a resource (such as photos, description, and pricing) so that I can make an informed decision about whether to book it.\n3. Check Resource Availability: As a customer, I want to be able to check the availability of a resource at a specific date and time so that I can ensure it is available before I make a booking.\n4. Make a Booking: As a customer, I want to be able to make a booking for a specific resource at a specific date and time, and include details such as the number of guests and any special requests.\n5. View Booking Details: As a customer, I want to be able to view the details of my bookings, including the resource, date, and time, so that I can see the details of my upcoming bookings.\n6. Cancel a Booking: As a customer, I want to be able to cancel a booking if I need to change my plans, and possibly able to see the cancellation policy\n7. View Resource Calendar: As an admin, I want to be able to view a calendar that displays the resources bookings, so that I can see the availability of resources at a glance.\n8. Manage Resources: As an admin, I want to be able to add, edit, and remove resources from the system, so that I can manage the resources that are available for booking.\n9. Manage Bookings: As an admin, I want to be able to view, edit, and delete bookings, as well as approve or deny pending bookings, so that I can manage the bookings that have been made.\n10. Manage Customers: As an admin, I want to be able to view, edit, and delete customer information, so that I can manage the customers who are making bookings.\n11. Send Confirmation Email: As a system, I want to be able to send an email confirmation after a customer makes a booking, so that the customer has a record of their booking.\n12. Payment Integration: As a customer, I want to be able to make payments for my bookings online, by using popular payment gateway like Stripe, PayPal or directly using Credit or Debit card\n13. Reporting: As an admin, I want to have the ability to access reports on the bookings made, resources booked, revenue generated, and customers who used the system.\n\nThis list of use cases covers the main functionalities that an online booking system should have. However, depending on your specific requirements, you may want to add or remove use cases as needed. It is also important to note that in addition to functional requirements, there should also be non-functional requirements such as performance, scalability, security and usability.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 0, 5692, 374, 264, 15817, 1140, 315, 990, 5048, 369, 458, 2860, 21857, 1849, 429, 14521, 5257, 13566, 315, 279, 1849, 1447, 16, 13, 7542, 16209, 25, 1634, 264, 6002, 11, 358, 1366, 311, 387, 2952, 311, 2711, 369, 2500, 4963, 320, 20805, 438, 9816, 12026, 11, 7096, 11, 476, 11474, 8, 3118, 389, 5257, 12890, 320, 20805, 438, 3728, 11, 8654, 11, 323, 943, 8, 773, 429, 358, 646, 1477, 279, 4963, 429, 3367, 847, 3880, 624, 17, 13, 2738, 11765, 12309, 25, 1634, 264, 6002, 11, 358, 1366, 3