INFO 03-13 07:54:11 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-3fb4cfb1c7bf44faa6aa28b2c9d1c17f-0: prompt: 'Jacob stood there, stunned, as Eri and Lorelei continued their intense fight. As he watched, he saw something he never thought possible - Lorelei was not the evil spirit he thought she was, but a benevolent one who had sustained the village for centuries. It was she who had kept him warm on the cold, snowy mountain when they first met. Before he could even process what was happening, he found himself yelling out to Eri.\n\n"Stop it!" Jacob yelled, his voice echoing in the air. "Leave her alone!"\n\nRacita looked at Jacob in horror, her eyes wide as she saw the boy she considered a friend turn against them. She tried to speak, to say something to stop him, but her voice failed her.\n\nLorelei, on the other hand, simply smirked. "Ah, the boy finally sees the truth," she said, her voice a purr. "I have been trying to tell you all along, but no one would listen."\n\nEri looked over at Jacob, confusion written all over his face. "What are you talking about, Jacob? She\'s a monster!"\n\nJacob shook his head. "No, she\'s not! She\'s been helping us all this time, Eri. Can\'t you see that?"\n\nRacita finally found her voice, her voice shaking as she spoke. "Jacob, she\'s using you! She\'s lying!"\n\nBut Jacob wouldn\'t listen, and before anyone could stop him, he was walking toward Lorelei, his hand outstretched.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [94167, 14638, 1052, 11, 46926, 11, 438, 468, 461, 323, 53233, 62785, 8570, 862, 18894, 4367, 13, 1634, 566, 15384, 11, 5