INFO 03-13 07:54:12 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-91fcb37a2c1c47de885f8e0426b554f2-0: prompt: 'If the "Load More" button is not appearing when you scroll to the bottom of the table, it\'s possible that there\'s an issue with the JavaScript code that\'s responsible for detecting when the user has reached the end of the table.\n\nHere\'s an example code snippet that you can use to detect when the user has scrolled to the bottom of the table and display the "Load More" button:\n```javascript\nconst table = document.getElementById(\'myTable\');\nlet currentPage = 1;\n\ntable.addEventListener(\'scroll\', () => {\n  // Calculate the distance between the bottom of the table and the bottom of the scrollable area\n  const distanceFromBottom = table.scrollHeight - table.scrollTop - table.clientHeight;\n\n  // If the user has scrolled to the bottom, show the "Load More" button\n  if (distanceFromBottom < 1) {\n    const loadMoreRow = document.createElement(\'tr\');\n    loadMoreRow.innerHTML = \'<td colspan="4"><button id="loadMoreButton">Load More</button></td>\';\n    table.querySelector(\'tbody\').appendChild(loadMoreRow);\n\n    const loadMoreButton = document.getElementById(\'loadMoreButton\');\n    loadMoreButton.addEventListener(\'click\', () => {\n      currentPage++;\n      loadMoreData(currentPage);\n    });\n  }\n});\n\nfunction loadMoreData(page) {\n  // Fetch the next page of data from the API and append it to the table\n  fetch(`https://www.example.com/load?page=${page}`)\n    .then(response => response.json())\n    .then(data => {\n      const rows = data.map(item => {\n        const row = document.createElement(\'tr\');\n        row.innerHTML = `<td>${item.column1}</td><td>${item.column2}</td><td>${item.column3}</td><td>${item.column4}</td>`;\n        return row;\n      });\n      table.querySelector(\'tbody\').append(...rows);\n    })\n    .catch(error => {\n      console.error(\'Error fetching data:\', error);\n    });\n}\n```\nThis code attaches a `scroll` event listener to the table element, which is triggered whenever the user scrolls within the table. When the user reaches the bottom of the table, it adds a new row to the table containing the "Load More" button. When the button is clicked, it increments the `currentPage` variable and calls the `loadMoreData` function to fetch the next page of data from the API and append it to the table.\n\nMake sure to replace the API URL in the `fetch` calls with your own URL, and adjust the code to match your specific table structure and data format.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2679, 279, 330, 5879, 4398, 1, 3137, 374, 537, 25377, 979, 498, 9059, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1965, 11, 432, 594, 3204, 429, 1052, 594, 458, 4265, 448, 279, 12914, 2038, 429, 594, 8480, 369, 53526, 979, 279, 1196, 702, 8643, 279, 835, 315, 279, 1965, 382, 8420, 594, 458, 3110, 2038, 43065, 429, 498, 646, 990, 311, 11140, 979, 279, 1196, 702, 95619, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1965, 323, 3037, 279, 330, 5879, 4398, 1, 3137, 510, 73594, 14073, 198, 1024, 1965, 284, 2197, 4749, 492, 2408, 2556, 1157, 1149, 39314, 284, 220, 16, 401, 2005, 10634, 492, 12605, 516, 1719, 589, 341, 220, 442, 20517, 279, 6010, 1948, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1965, 323, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 9059, 480, 3082, 198, 220, 733, 6010, 3830, 11279, 284, 1965, 90859, 481, 1965, 48546, 481, 1965, 74311, 401, 220, 442, 1416, 279, 1196, 702, 95619, 311, 279, 5622, 11, 1473, 279, 330, 5879, 4398, 1, 3137, 198, 220, 421, 320, 19348, 3830, 11279, 366, 220, 16, 8, 341, 262, 733, 2795, 7661, 3102, 284, 2197, 9732, 492, 376, 1157, 26