INFO 03-13 07:54:15 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-2b0497b424944381bfb52747cc1ac70c-0: prompt: "Here are the next 10 lines of code for the controller action that generates the RSS feed content from the Instagram feed posts in the database:\n```\n        // Add an item element for each post\n        foreach ($posts as $post) {\n            $rssContent .= '<item>';\n            $rssContent .= '<title>' . $post->link . '</title>';\n            $rssContent .= '<link>' . $post->link . '</link>';\n            $rssContent .= '<description>' . $post->type . '</description>';\n            $rssContent .= '<pubDate>' . $post->created_at->toRssString() . '</pubDate>';\n            $rssContent .= '<guid>' . $post->link . '</guid>';\n            $rssContent .= '</item>';\n        }\n\n        $rssContent .= '</channel>';\n        $rssContent .= '</rss>';\n\n        // Return the RSS feed content as an application/rss+xml response\n        return response($rssContent, 200)\n            ->header('Content-Type', 'application/rss+xml');\n    }\n}\n```\nThis code generates an `item` element for each post in the `$posts` collection and adds the `title`, `link`, `description`, `pubDate`, and `guid` elements to the `item` element. The `title` element contains the link to the post, the `link` element contains the link to the post, the `description` element contains the type of the post (photo or video), the `pubDate` element contains the creation date of the post, and the `guid` element contains the link to the post.\n\nFinally, the code closes the `channel` and `rss` elements and returns the RSS feed content as an `application/rss+xml` response.\n\nI hope this helps. Let me know if you have any more questions.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_token