INFO 03-13 07:54:15 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-caf9122debd34ebd937f014bde5fc543-0: prompt: '11. Notifications Table:\n```\nCREATE TABLE notifications (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    tenant_id INT NOT NULL,\n    message VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    status BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,\n    FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id) REFERENCES tenants (id)\n);\n```\nThis table can be used to store notifications for tenants, such as upcoming rent payments, lease renewals, and maintenance schedules. The "status" column can be used to indicate if the notification has been read or not. This table can be used to send automated notifications to tenants, reminding them of important dates, and keeping them updated with the latest information regarding their rental property.\n\n12. Documents Table:\n```\nCREATE TABLE documents (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    tenant_id INT NOT NULL,\n    document_name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    file_path VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,\n    FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id) REFERENCES tenants (id)\n);\n```\nThis table can be used to store documents related to tenants, such as pay stubs, income verification, and lease agreements. The "file\\_path" column can be used to store the path to the document file, which can be a link to a cloud storage service. This table can be used to make it easy for landlords to access important documents and validate tenant information.\n\nAs always, please keep in mind that these tables are examples, and you may need to modify them according to your specific needs and the size of your data, also you will need to take into account the security and the cost of the service you are going to use.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=N