INFO 03-13 07:54:17 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-41bb4265b1e74c59a086eded0910ae5f-0: prompt: 'Yes, I can suggest a few additional improvements:\n\n1. Implement an asynchronous version of the smart order routing function to take full advantage of the asynchronous nature of price fetching and other operations.\n2. Add a mechanism to automatically refresh cached fees and latencies after a certain period of time.\n3. Replace the default `Queue` with an `asyncio.Queue` to allow for better async handling.\n\nHere\'s the updated code with these improvements:\n\nPart 1 remains the same.\n\nPart 2:\n```python\nfrom functools import partial\n\nclass Exchange(ABC):\n    # ... (Previous code remains the same)\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def fetch_price(self, trading_pair):\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def start_real_time_feed(self, trading_pair):\n        pass\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def get_fee(self, amount, refresh=False):\n        if refresh:\n            self.get_fee.cache_clear()\n        # Implement logic to fetch and return the fee\n        pass\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def get_latency(self, refresh=False):\n        if refresh:\n            self.get_latency.cache_clear()\n        # Implement logic to fetch and return the latency\n        pass\n\n    async def update_price(self, trading_pair, price_queue, max_retries=3):\n        # ... (Update price method remains the same)\n\n    def is_healthy(self):\n        return self._is_healthy\n\n# Implement specific exchange classes like Binance, Coinbase, and Kraken here\n```\nPart 3:\n```python\nasync def update_prices_worker_async(exchanges, trading_pair, price_queue):\n    tasks = [exchange.update_price(trading_pair, price_queue) for exchange in exchanges]\n    await asyncio.gather(*tasks)\n\nasync def smart_order_routing_async(order, trading_pair, exchanges, routing_strategy, custom_routing_function=None, **kwargs):\n    price_queue = asyncio.Queue()\n\n    healthy_exchanges = [exchange for exchange in exchanges if exchange.is_healthy()]\n    await update_prices_worker_async(healthy_exchanges, trading_pair, price_queue)\n\n    if routing_strategy == "custom":\n        selected_exchange, selected_price = custom_routing(order, price_queue, **kwargs)\n    else:\n        selected_exchange, selected_price = None, None\n\n    if selected_exchange and selected_price:\n        order.exchange = selected_exchange.name\n        order.price = selected_price\n        order.status = "executed"\n    else:\n        order.status = "failed"\n\n    return order\n\n# ... (Previous code remains the same)\n```\nPart 4:\n```python\n# Initialize Configuration Manager\nconfig_manager = ConfigManager("config.ini")\n\n# Define exchanges\nbinance_credentials = config_manager.get_exchange_credentials("Binance")\nbinance = Binance(binance_credentials["api_key"], binance_credentials["api_secret"])\n\n# Add other exchanges like Coinbase and Kraken here\n\nexchanges = [binance]  # Add other exchanges to the list\n\n# Define order\norder = Order("BTCUSD", 1, "buy")\n\n# Update initial prices\ntrading_pairs = config_manager.get_trading_pairs()\n\nfor trading_pair in trading_pairs:\n    routing_strategy = "custom"\n    custom_routing_fn = partial(custom_routing, weight_fees=0.5, weight_latency=0.5)\n\n    loop = asyncio.get_event_loop()\n    executed_order = loop.run_until_complete(smart_order_routing_async(order, trading_pair, exchanges, routing_strategy, custom_routing_function=custom_routing_fn))\n\n    # Print the result\n    print(executed_order)\n```\nThese improvements include an asynchronous version of the smart order routing function, a mechanism to automatically refresh cached fees and latencies, and a replacement of the default `Queue` with an `asyncio.Queue` for', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_wor