INFO 03-13 07:54:19 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-244faa1bdf5e47a789b20c7d01b86d5f-0: prompt: 'Mobile cloud computing refers to the use of cloud computing technology to provide services to mobile devices such as smartphones and tablets. While mobile cloud computing has several benefits such as increased storage capacity, improved processing power, and reduced battery usage, it also has some shortcomings.\n\nOne major shortcoming of mobile devices for mobile cloud computing is limited battery life. Mobile devices are designed to be energy efficient and have limited battery capacity. Running cloud-based applications on mobile devices can drain the battery quickly, reducing the amount of time the user can use the device without recharging it.\n\nAnother shortcoming of mobile devices for mobile cloud computing is limited network connectivity. Mobile devices rely on wireless network connections such as Wi-Fi, 4G, and 5G to access cloud services. However, network coverage can be limited or inconsistent in some areas, leading to slow or unreliable connections. This can affect the user experience and limit the usefulness of cloud-based services.\n\nDistance clouds, on the other hand, suffer from the latency problem. Since the mobile device needs to communicate with the cloud server over a network, there is a delay in processing and response time. This delay can be significant, especially for applications that require real-time responses. This delay can make mobile cloud computing unsuitable for certain applications such as online gaming, video conferencing, and real-time data processing.\n\nIn summary, the major shortcomings of mobile devices and distance clouds for mobile cloud computing are limited battery life, limited network connectivity, and latency. These issues can affect the user experience and limit the usefulness of cloud-based services. To overcome these challenges, mobile cloud computing providers need to focus on optimizing energy consumption, improving network connectivity, and reducing latency.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [18370, 9437, 24231, 19257, 311, 279, 990, 315, 9437, 24231, 5440, 311, 3410, 3516, 311, 6371, 7611, 1741, 438, 35022, 323, 28579, 13, 5976, 6371, 9437, 24231, 702, 3807, 7567, 1741, 438, 7172, 5819, 8654, 11, 12944, 8692, 2355, 11, 323, 11046, 11602, 10431, 11, 432, 1083, 702, 1045, 71921, 382, 3966, 3598, 2805, 4959, 315, 6371, 7611, 369, 6371, 9437, 24231, 374, 7199, 11602, 2272, 13, 13411, 7611, 525, 6188, 311, 387, 4802, 11050, 323, 614, 7199, 11602, 8654, 13, 28025, 9437, 5980, 8357, 389, 6371, 7611, 646, 23727, 279, 11602, 6157, 11, 17719, 279, 3311, 315, 882, 279, 1196, 646, 990, 279, 3671, 2041, 312, 62359, 432, 382, 14037, 2805, 4959, 315, 6371, 7611, 369, 6371, 9437, 24231, 374, 7199, 3922, 30257, 13, 13411, 7611, 17188, 389, 20739, 3922, 13234, 1741, 438, 17220, 26299, 11, 220, 19, 38, 11, 323, 220, 20, 38, 311, 2615, 9437, 3516, 13, 4354, 11, 3922, 10191, 646, 387, 7199, 476, 39140, 304, 1045, 5671, 11, 6388, 311, 6301, 476, 66029, 13234, 13, 1096, 646, 7802, 279, 1196, 3139, 323, 3930, 279, 75864, 315, 9437, 5980, 3516, 382, 14778, 29514, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 7676, 504, 279, 39270, 3491, 13, 8704, 279, 6371, 3671, 3880, 311, 19032, 448, 279, 9437, 3538, 916, 264, 3922, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 7626, 304, 8692, 323, 2033, 882, 13, 1096, 7626, 646, 387, 5089, 11, 5310, 369, 8357, 429, 1373, 1931, 7246, 14507, 13, 1096, 7626, 646, 1281, 6371, 9437, 24231, 6975, 85481, 369, 3654, 8357, 1741, 438, 2860, 15833, 11, 2766, 48743, 11373, 11, 323, 1931, 7246, 821, 8692, 38