INFO 03-13 07:54:22 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-6fc702d3088e4247a88dc4def5b4faae-0: prompt: 'To implement the GCP-specific logic to listen for termination events, you can use the Google Cloud Python SDK to interact with Google Compute Engine (GCE) and Google Cloud Pub/Sub. This example demonstrates setting up a Pub/Sub topic to listen for Preemptible VM instance terminations and forwarding the events to the FastAPI WebSocket.\n\n1. Update the GCP termination monitor to include the necessary functions (`cloud_providers/gcp_termination_monitor.py`):\n```python\nfrom google.cloud import compute_v1, pubsub_v1\nfrom google.oauth2 import service_account\nfrom fastapi import WebSocket\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom .termination_monitor import AbstractTerminationMonitor\n\nclass GCPTerminationMonitor(AbstractTerminationMonitor):\n    def __init__(self, project_id: str, region: str, zone: str, credentials_path: str, pubsub_topic: str):\n        self.project_id = project_id\n        self.region = region\n        self.zone = zone\n        self.pubsub_topic = pubsub_topic\n\n        credentials = service_account.Credentials.from_service_account_file(\n            credentials_path\n        )\n        self.subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient(credentials=credentials)\n\n    async def listen_for_termination(self, websocket: WebSocket):\n        # Subscribe the WebSocket to the Pub/Sub topic\n        self._subscribe_websocket_to_pubsub_topic(websocket)\n\n    def _subscribe_websocket_to_pubsub_topic(self, websocket: WebSocket):\n        def handle_pubsub_message(message):\n            termination_time = message.attributes["preemptible-vm-shutdown"]\n            instance_id = message.attributes["instance-id"]\n            event = {\n                "event": "termination_warning",\n                "instance_id": instance_id,\n                "termination_time": termination_time,\n            }\n            websocket.send_text(json.dumps(event))\n\n        subscription_path = self.subscriber.subscription_path(\n            self.project_id, "termination_events"\n        )\n\n        # Process messages from the Pub/Sub topic\n        while True:\n            response = self.subscriber.pull(subscription_path, max_messages=1)\n            for msg in response.received_messages:\n                self.subscriber.acknowledge(subscription_path, [msg.ack_id])\n                handle_pubsub_message(msg.message)\n```\n1. Update `main.py` to include the Pub/Sub topic:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, WebSocket\n# ... other imports ...\nfrom cloud_providers.gcp_termination_monitor import GCPTerminationMonitor\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Initialize the termination monitor\ntermination_monitor = GCPTerminationMonitor(\n    project_id="YOUR_PROJECT_ID",\n    region="us-west1",\n    zone="us-west1-a",\n    credentials_path="path/to/credentials.json",\n    pubsub_topic="termination_events"\n)\n\n# ... other code ...\n```\nThis implementation updates the `GCPTerminationMonitor` class to subscribe the WebSocket to a Pub/Sub topic that will receive termination event notifications. The `_subscribe_websocket_to_pubsub_topic` method handles subscribing the WebSocket to the Pub/Sub topic and processing incoming messages.\n\nPlease note that this example assumes you have already set up a Pub/Sub topic to receive Preemptible VM instance termination events. If you haven\'t already set up the topic, you can follow the steps in the [official GCP documentation](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/preemptible#detecting_if_an_instance_was_preempted).\n\nAdditionally, note that the provided implementation uses a WebSocket to receive termination events directly from the GCP Pub/Sub topic, which is not natively supported. In a production environment, you would typically use an intermediary service, like a Cloud Function or an API Gateway, to forward Pub/Sub notifications to the WebSocket.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [1249, 4211, 279, 479, 7123, 18906, 12218, 311, 8844, 369, 34408, 4357, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 5085, 14817, 13027, 26623, 311, 16282, 448, 5085, 22603, 8200, 320, 38, 2104, 8, 323, 5085, 14817, 22611, 49972, 13, 1096, 3110, 31116, 6243, 705, 264, 22611, 49972, 8544, 311, 8844, 369, 4968, 20968, 1238, 17792, 2867, 10204, 804, 323, 62104, 279, 4357, 311, 279, 17288, 7082, 47042, 382, 16, 13, 5549, 279, 479, 7123, 34408, 8718, 311, 2924, 279, 5871, 5746, 28654, 12361, 2540, 17761, 4846, 4672, 62, 88676, 40112, 7197, 63, 982, 73594, 12669, 198, 1499, 11558, 16935, 1159, 12564, 2273, 16, 11, 6675, 1966, 2273, 16, 198, 1499, 11558, 57773, 17, 1159, 2473, 13500, 198, 1499, 4937, 2068, 1159, 47042, 198, 474, 2951, 198, 474, 2643, 198, 1499, 659, 88676, 40112, 1159, 13513, 21209, 32096, 30098, 271, 1040, 22381, 2828, 261, 32096, 30098, 77219, 21209, 32096, 30098, 982, 262, 707, 1304, 2327, 3804, 721, 11, 2390, 842, 25, 607, 11, 5537, 25, 607, 11, 10143, 25, 607, 11, 16387, 2638, 25, 607, 11, 6675, 1966, 31414, 25, 607, 982, 286, 656, 14504, 842, 284, 2390, 842, 198, 286, 656, 42976, 284, 5537, 198, 286, 656, 57808, 284, 10143, 198, 286, 656, 47773, 1966, 31414, 284, 6675, 1966, 31414, 271, 286, 16387, 284, 2473, 13500, 727, 15735, 6387, 12267, 13500, 2458, 1006, 310, 16387, 2638, 198, 286, 1727, 286, 656, 4309, 20351, 284, 6675, 1966, 2273, 16, 12391, 20351, 2959, 85465, 28, 32353, 692, 262, 3312, 707, 8844, 5478, 62, 88676, 1193, 11, 58943, 25, 47042, 982, 286, 671, 27270, 279, 47042, 311, 279, 22611, 49972, 8544, 198, 286, 656, 1436, 9384, 25960, 9556, 2346, 34014, 1966, 31414, 39769, 9556, 692, 