INFO 03-13 07:54:23 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-f29c4ab58a3e4d508ff3af27c6b3b84e-0: prompt: "Sure, here's an example of how the workshops could be structured based on symptoms:\n\n  Copy Table\n\n| Symptom | Likely Cause | Objective | Insights | Potential Activities |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Nervousness | Mindset and Unclear Objectives | Encourage founders to identify their personal why for starting their business and clarify their objectives for pitching. | - Tapping into intrinsic motivation can help communicate passion more effectively. - Clear objectives can help reduce nerves by providing focus. | - Have founders write down their personal why statement and share it with the group. - Have founders clarify their objectives and practice incorporating them into their pitch. |\n| Lack of Authenticity | Fear of Showing Weakness | Discuss the importance of authenticity in pitching and encourage founders to be honest about their strengths and weaknesses. | - Authenticity builds trust with investors and potential partners. - Vulnerability can be a strength in pitching. | - Have founders identify their strengths and weaknesses and practice incorporating them into their pitch. - Have founders share a personal story that shows vulnerability and authenticity. |\n| Difficulty Engaging Audience | Lack of Connection to Audience | Provide tips on how to connect with the audience and encourage founders to research their audience. | - Connecting with the audience can help keep them interested and invested. - Understanding the audience's interests and needs can help tailor the pitch. | - Have founders research the audience they will be pitching to and tailor their pitch accordingly. - Practice using storytelling and interactive elements to engage the audience. |\n| Poor Body Language | Lack of Confidence | Discuss the importance of body language in pitching and encourage founders to practice confident body language. | - Confident body language can convey confidence and engagement. - Practicing confident body language can help build confidence. | - Practice maintaining eye contact, using gestures, and standing with confidence. - Have founders practice power poses to increase confidence. |\n| Lack of Clarity | Unclear Objectives and Message | Provide guidance on clarifying objectives and structuring the pitch. | - A clear message can help avoid confusing the audience. - A clear structure can help keep the pitch organized and easy to follow. | - Provide a template for structuring a pitch and have founders practice using it. - Have founders practice summarizing their main points concisely. |\n| Difficulty Sticking to Time Limit | Lack of Practice and Unclear Objectives | Encourage founders to practice their pitch with a timer and clarify their objectives for pitching. | - Practicing with a timer can help keep the pitch concise and avoid going off-topic. - Clear objectives can help reduce nerves by providing focus. | - Have founders practice their pitch with a timer and provide feedback on timing. - Have founders clarify their objectives and practice incorporating them into their pitch. |\n\nIn this structure, the symptoms that startup founders typically experience when it comes to pitching are identified, and each section is designed to address the likely cause of the symptom. The objective, insights, and potential activities for each section are tailored to help founders overcome the underlying cause and improve their pitch.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 1588, 594, 458, 3110, 315, 1246, 279, 34836, 1