INFO 03-13 07:54:26 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-4b0571ea92ac48afbf600125d1433706-0: prompt: 'Sure, the `frame.append()` method is deprecated in the latest version of pandas. Instead, we can use the `concat()` function to concatenate the rows to the dataframe. Here\'s the updated code:\n```python\nfrom PyPDF2 import PdfReader\nimport pandas as pd\nimport re\nimport os\n\n# Define the chunk size\nchunk_size = 500\n\n# Create an empty list to store the text chunks\ntext_chunks = []\n\n# Define the filename without extension\nfilename = os.path.splitext("python_tutorial.pdf")[0]\n\n# Open the PDF file\nwith open("python_tutorial.pdf", "rb") as file:\n    # Create a PdfReader object from the file\n    reader = PdfReader(file)\n\n    # Loop over each page in the PDF document\n    for page in reader.pages:\n        # Extract the text from the page\n        text = page.extract_text()\n\n        # Split the text into chunks of the specified size\n        chunks = [text[i:i+chunk_size] for i in range(0, len(text), chunk_size)]\n\n        # Clean up the special characters in each chunk\n        clean_chunks = [re.sub(r"[^a-zA-Z0-9]+", " ", chunk) for chunk in chunks]\n\n        # Add the clean chunks to the text_chunks list\n        text_chunks.extend(clean_chunks)\n\n# Create a pandas dataframe to store the text chunks\ndf = pd.DataFrame(columns=["filename", "text"])\n\n# Loop over each clean chunk and append it to the dataframe if it is not empty\nfor i, chunk in enumerate(text_chunks):\n    if chunk.strip():  # check if the chunk is not empty\n        row = {"filename": filename, "text": chunk}\n        df = pd.concat([df, pd.DataFrame(row, index=[i])])\n\n# Print the dataframe\nprint(df.head())\n```\nIn this updated code, we first define the chunk size and create an empty list called `text_chunks` to store the text chunks.\n\nWe then define the filename without extension using the `os.path.splitext()` function, open the PDF file using the `open()` function with the read-binary mode, and create a `PdfReader` object from the file using the `PdfReader()` function.\n\nWe then loop over each page in the PDF document, extract the text from the page, split the text into chunks of the specified size, clean up the special characters in each chunk, and add the clean chunks to the `text_chunks` list.\n\nNext, we create an empty pandas dataframe called `df` with two columns `"filename"` and `"text"` using the `pd.DataFrame()` function with the `columns` parameter.\n\nWe then loop over each clean chunk in the `text_chunks` list using a `for` loop with the `enumerate()` function to get the index `i` and the chunk `chunk`. We check if the chunk is not empty using the `strip()` method, which removes any leading or trailing whitespace characters and returns an empty string if the chunk is empty. If the chunk is not empty, we create a dictionary `row` with the `filename` and `chunk` values, and then create a new dataframe with this row using the `pd.DataFrame()` function with the `index` parameter set to `[i]`. We then concatenate this new dataframe to the `df` dataframe using the `pd.concat()` function with the `axis=0` parameter.\n\nFinally, we print the first few rows of the dataframe using the `head()` method. This should exclude any empty text chunks from the dataframe and avoid the warning about the `frame.append()` method being deprecated.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 279, 1565, 6763, 2057, 54258, 1714, 374, 31590, 304, 279, 5535, 2319, 315, 18617, 13, 12090, 11, 582, 646, 990, 279, 1565, 20164, 54258, 729, 311