INFO 03-13 07:54:28 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-ffdb9728b8cf48fd898bb822bc5f3751-0: prompt: 'Scented videos are a type of immersive advertising that allows viewers to experience the scent of a fragrance while watching a video on their computer or mobile device. The technology behind scented videos involves using a small device that emits scents or a scented strip or card that is attached to the screen.\n\nThe device can be connected to the computer or mobile device through USB, Bluetooth or other means, and the scent can be released at different points during the video, depending on the brand\'s objectives. For example, the scent can be released at the beginning of the video to grab the viewer\'s attention, or during key moments in the video to enhance the emotional impact of the message.\n\nThe scented strip or card works by using micro-encapsulation technology to trap tiny droplets of fragrance oil within a polymer matrix. When the strip or card is rubbed or scratched, the droplets are released and the scent is activated.\n\nScented videos have been used by fragrance brands to create more engaging and immersive advertising experiences, and to showcase the scent of a fragrance in a way that traditional video or print advertisements cannot. They have also been used to reach a wider and more diverse audience, as they do not require consumers to visit a physical store to experience the fragrance.\n\nOne example of a brand that has used scented videos is Kenzo Parfums, which created a scented video for its fragrance "Kenzo World" in 2017. The video featured a dancer surrounded by flowers, and the viewer could scratch a scented card attached to the screen to experience the fragrance of the perfume.\n\nWhile scented videos are still a relatively new and niche technology, they represent an innovative and creative way for fragrance brands to connect with consumers and enhance the sensory experience of their products.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0