INFO 03-13 07:54:30 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-a30e937343d34545ad2c1a66cf1f86dd-0: prompt: "Sure, here's an example of adding obstacle avoidance to the drone's navigation system:\n```python\nimport cv2\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass Drone:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.position = [0, 0, 0]\n        self.velocity = [0, 0, 0]\n        self.acceleration = [0, 0, 0]\n        self.destination = [0, 0, 0]\n        self.obstacles = []\n\n    def navigate(self):\n        # Obstacle avoidance logic\n        for obstacle in self.obstacles:\n            distance_to_obstacle = np.linalg.norm(np.array(self.position) - np.array(obstacle.position))\n            if distance_to_obstacle < obstacle.radius:\n                # Avoid the obstacle by changing the drone's direction\n                self.velocity = np.array(obstacle.position) - np.array(self.position)\n                self.velocity /= np.linalg.norm(self.velocity)\n                self.velocity *= obstacle.radius - distance_to_obstacle\n\n        # Move the drone towards its destination\n        direction_to_destination = np.array(self.destination) - np.array(self.position)\n        self.acceleration = direction_to_destination\n        self.velocity += self.acceleration\n        self.position += self.velocity\n\nclass Obstacle:\n    def __init__(self, position, radius):\n        self.position = position\n        self.radius = radius\n\n# Example usage\ndrone1 = Drone()\ndrone2 = Drone()\n\nobstacle1 = Obstacle([10, 10, 0], 5)\nobstacle2 = Obstacle([20, 20, 0], 3)\n\ndrone1.obstacles = [obstacle1, obstacle2]\ndrone2.obstacles = [obstacle2]\n\ndrone1.destination = [30, 30, 0]\ndrone2.destination = [15, 15, 0]\n\nfor i in range(100):\n    drone1.navigate()\n    drone2.navigate()\n\n    # Display the drones and obstacles on a map\n    map_image = np.zeros((50, 50, 3), np.uint8)\n    cv2.circle(map_image, (int(drone1.position[0]), int(drone1.position[1])), 2, (0, 0, 255), -1)\n    cv2.circle(map_image, (int(drone2.position[0]), int(drone2.position[1])), 2, (255, 0, 0), -1)\n    cv2.circle(map_image, (int(obstacle1.position[0]), int(obstacle1.position[1])), obstacle1.radius, (0, 255, 0), -1)\n    cv2.circle(map_image, (int(obstacle2.position[0]), int(obstacle2.position[1])), obstacle2.radius, (0, 255, 0), -1)\n    cv2.imshow('Map', map_image)\n    cv2.waitKey(50)\n\ncv2.destroyAllWindows()\n```\nIn this example, we have added a list of obstacles to each drone object, and modified the `navigate` method to include obstacle avoidance logic. The drone checks its distance to each obstacle and changes its velocity to avoid collision. We have also added a simple visualization of the drones and obstacles on a map using OpenCV.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 1588, 594, 458, 3110, 315, 7842, 32187, 64311, 311, 279, 26713, 594, 10646, 1849, 510, 73594, 12669, 198, 474, 5544, 17, 198, 474, 8591, 438, 2595, 271, 1040, 73481, 510, 262, 707, 1304, 2327, 3804, 721, 982, 286, 656, 6187, 284, 508, 15, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 921, 286, 656, 25390, 284, 508, 15, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 921, 286, 656, 77992, 20927, 284, 508, 15, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 921, 286, 656, 35018, 284, 508, 15, 11, 220, 15, 11, 220, 15, 921, 286, 656, 26605, 73979, 284, 14599, 262, 707, 20876, 1193, 982, 286, 671, 4657, 43598, 64311, 12218, 198, 286, 369, 32187, 304, 656, 26605, 73979, 510, 310, 6010, 2346, 36322, 43598, 284, 2595, 37732, 31964, 9900, 7234, 1193, 6187, 8, 481, 2595, 7234, 49595, 43598, 6187, 1171, 310, 421, 6010, 2346, 36322, 43598, 366, 32187, 34094, 510, 394, 671, 34006