INFO 03-13 07:54:32 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-15a35aab20334ec0bb460c8cb32529a4-0: prompt: "It's possible that the inner join with `vStudentParents` is causing duplicates in the `Students` column. To fix this, you can try grouping the query by the `UserId`, `ParentUniqueId`, `Login`, `scr.ParentCode`, `Addressee`, `AddressNumber`, `Salutation`, `PreferredName`, `Surname`, and `Email` columns, and applying the `STRING_AGG` function to the `sp.StudentCode` column within each group.\n\nHere's an updated version of the query with the suggested modifications:\n```sql\nSELECT\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2' END AS UserId,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2' END AS ParentUniqueId,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2' END AS Login,\n    STRING_AGG(CONVERT(NVARCHAR(max), sp.StudentCode), ',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY sp.StudentCode) AS Students,\n    scr.ParentCode,\n    Addressee,\n    AddressNumber,\n    Salutation,\n    'Parent - ' + Salutation AS UserInternalDisplayName,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN MPreferredName WHEN '6' THEN FPreferredName END AS PreferredName,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN MSurname WHEN '6' THEN FSurname END AS Surname,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.Email WHEN '6' THEN Email2 END AS Email,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1@parent.sthildas.qld.edu.au' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2@parent.sthildas.qld.edu.au' END AS UserPrincipalName\nFROM TASS_StudentDetails_CommunicationRulesDetails scr\nINNER JOIN TASS_IDM_Parents p\n    ON p.UserCode = scr.ParentCode\nLEFT JOIN vStudentParents sp\n    ON sp.ParentUniqueID = p.UniqueID\nWHERE \n    ((AddressNumber = '5' AND scr.Email <>'' AND scr.Email NOT LIKE '%@sthildas.qld.edu.au%' AND p.SplitFamilyNumber NOT IN ('1','2')) OR (AddressNumber = '6' AND Email2 <>'' AND Email2 NOT LIKE '%@sthildas.qld.edu.au%' AND p.SplitFamilyNumber NOT IN ('1','2'))) \n    AND CommunicationType like '%GEN%'\n    AND AddressNumber in ('5','6')\nGROUP BY \n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2' END,\n    scr.ParentCode,\n    Addressee,\n    AddressNumber,\n    Salutation,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN MPreferredName WHEN '6' THEN FPreferredName END,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN MSurname WHEN '6' THEN FSurname END,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.Email WHEN '6' THEN Email2 END,\n    CASE AddressNumber WHEN '5' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_1@parent.sthildas.qld.edu.au' WHEN '6' THEN scr.ParentCode + '_2@parent.sthildas.qld.edu.au' END\n```\nIn this updated query, the `LEFT JOIN` with `vStudentParents` returns `NULL` values for the `sp.StudentCode` column when there are no matching rows in `vStudentParents`. The `STRING_AGG` function is then applied within each group", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2132, 594, 3204, 429, 279, 9179, 5138, 448, 1565, 85, 14096, 61769, 63, 374, 14381, 42328, 304, 279, 1565, 30952, 63, 3250, 13, 2014, 5046, 419, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 49184, 279, 3239, 553, 279, 1565, 13504, 7808, 1565, 8387, 72498, 7808, 1565, 6231, 7808, 1565, 25065, 28985, 2078, 7808, 1565, 2212, 416, 4060, 7808, 1565, 4286, 2833, 7808, 1565, 17245, 22705, 7808, 1565, 22482, 675, 7808, 1565, 81230, 7808, 323, 1565, 4781, 63, 8147, 11, 323, 18950, 279, 1565, 16468, 1566, 22254, 63, 729, 311, 279, 1565, 2154, 56876, 2078, 63, 3250, 2878, 1817, 1874, 382, 8420, 594, 458, 