INFO 03-13 07:54:32 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-13386d3fc8b44b7683be1ff520443764-0: prompt: 'I apologize for the mistake in my previous answer. Here\'s an updated implementation that correctly updates the players\' scores (`p1_points` and `p2_points`) based on the outcome of each point, and updates the game score (`score`) based on the outcome of each game:\n```R\n# Set the initial score to 0-0\nscore <- c(0, 0)\n\n# Set the probabilities of winning a point on serve and on return for each player\np1_serve <- 0.6\np1_return <- 0.4\np2_serve <- 0.5\np2_return <- 0.5\n\n# Simulate a match until one player wins 2 sets\nwhile (max(score) < 2) {\n  # Alternate the serve between players at the start of each game\n  if (sum(score) %% 4 == 0 || sum(score) %% 4 == 3) {\n    serving_player <- 1\n  } else {\n    serving_player <- 2\n  }\n  \n  # Simulate a game\n  p1_points <- 0\n  p2_points <- 0\n  while (abs(p1_points - p2_points) < 2 || max(p1_points, p2_points) < 4) {\n    # Determine the probability of winning the point based on the serving player\n    if (serving_player == 1) {\n      p_serve <- p1_serve\n      p_return <- p2_return\n    } else {\n      p_serve <- p2_serve\n      p_return <- p1_return\n    }\n    \n    # Simulate a point\n    if (runif(1) < p_serve) {\n      # The serving player wins the point\n      if (runif(1) < p_return) {\n        # The returning player fails to return the serve\n        p1_points <- p1_points + 1\n      }\n    } else {\n      # The returning player wins the point\n      if (runif(1) < p_serve) {\n        # The serving player fails to return the serve\n        p2_points <- p2_points + 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  \n  # Update the score based on the winner of the game\n  if (p1_points > p2_points) {\n    score[1] <- score[1] + 1\n  } else {\n    score[2] <- score[2] + 1\n  }\n}\n\n# Print the final score of the match\nif (score[1] > score[2]) {\n  winner <- "Player 1"\n} else {\n  winner <- "Player 2"\n}\ncat("Final score:", score[1], "-", score[2], "(", winner, "wins)\\n")\n```\nAgain, I apologize for the mistake and I hope this corrected implementation helps.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [40, 36879, 369, 279, 16523, 304, 847, 3681, 4226, 13, 5692, 594, 458, 6049, 8129, 429, 12440, 8837, 279, 4217, 6, 12205, 28654, 79, 16, 12928, 63, 323, 1565, 79, 17, 12928, 32881, 3118, 389, 279, 15274, 315, 1817, 1459, 11, 323, 8837, 279, 1809, 5456, 28654, 12338, 32881, 3118, 389, 279, 15274, 315, 1817, 1809, 510, 73594, 49, 198, 2, 2573, 279, 2856, 5456, 311, 220, 15, 12, 15, 198, 12338, 9119, 272, 7, 15, 11, 220, 15, 692, 2, 2573, 279, 48216, 315, 10987, 264, 1459, 389, 8683, 323, 389, 470, 369, 1817, 2781, 198, 79, 16, 643, 5852, 9119, 220, 15, 13, 21, 198, 79, 16, 12511, 9119, 220, 15, 13, 19, 198, 79, 17, 643, 5852, 9119, 220, 15, 13, 20, 198, 79, 17, 12511, 9119, 220, 15, 13, 20, 271, 2, 4467, 6334, 264, 2432, 3080, 825, 2781, 14816, 220, 17, 7289, 198, 3472, 320, 2810, 34480, 8, 366, 220, 17, 8, 341, 220, 671, 74724, 279, 8683, 1948, 4217, 518, 279, 1191, 315, 1817, 1809, 198, 220, 421, 320, 1242, 34480, 8, 23277, 220, 19, 621, 220, 15, 1369, 2629, 34480, 8, 23277, 220, 19, 621, 220, 18, 8, 341, 262, 13480, 15524, 9119, 220, 16, 198, 220, 335, 770, 341, 262, 13480, 15524, 9119, 220, 17, 198, 220, 456, 2303, 220, 671, 4467, 6334, 264, 1809, 198, 220, 281, 16, 12928, 9119, 220, 15, 198, 220, 281, 17, 12928, 9119, 220, 15, 198, 220, 1393, 320, 3435, 1295, 16, 12928, 481, 281, 17, 12928, 8, 366, 220, 17, 1369, 1932, 1295, 16, 12928, 11, 281, 17, 12928, 8, 366, 220, 19, 8, 341, 262, 671