INFO 03-13 07:54:35 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-70d3651b4b544a9e80dd799396a9ae59-0: prompt: 'Here is an example of how you could create a Work Manager that mimics the current `TripDataSyncManager` that was running the `TripDataSyncTask`:\n```\nclass TripDataSyncManager(private val application: Application) {\n\n    fun startSync(userWifiPref: Boolean, userDataPref: Boolean) {\n        val workRequest = OneTimeWorkRequestBuilder<TripDataSyncWorker>()\n            .setInputData(workDataOf(\n                "userWifiPref" to userWifiPref,\n                "userDataPref" to userDataPref\n            ))\n            .setConstraints(\n                Constraints.Builder()\n                    .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.CONNECTED)\n                    .setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true)\n                    .build()\n            )\n            .build()\n\n        WorkManager.getInstance(application).enqueue(workRequest)\n    }\n}\n```\nYou can use this manager class to start the sync with the passed user preferences.\n```\nval manager = TripDataSyncManager(application)\nmanager.startSync(userWifiPref, userDataPref)\n```\nThe above code snippet is just an example and you may need to adjust it based on your specific requirements, and also add any additional functionality that you may need in your use case.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [8420, 374, 458, 3110, 315, 1246, 498, 1410, 1855, 264, 5547, 10567, 429, 26905, 1211, 279, 1482, 1565, 56352, 1043, 12154, 2043, 63, 429, 572, 4303, 279, 1565, 56352, 1043, 12154, 6262, 63, 510, 13874, 3989, 1040, 26