INFO 03-13 07:54:36 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-44b31336fea94d75a270c7e4a15c3691-0: prompt: 'This error occurs because the `SendMessage` API operation requires either Content-Based Deduplication or an explicit `MessageDeduplicationId` parameter when sending messages to a FIFO (First-In-First-Out) queue. FIFO queues are designed to preserve the order of messages and support message groups, which are batches of messages that belong to the same ordered group.\n\nIf Content-Based Deduplication is enabled, the system automatically deduplicates messages based on their content. Otherwise, you must provide an explicit `MessageDeduplicationId` parameter that identifies the message and enables deduplication.\n\nTo fix this error, you can either enable Content-Based Deduplication for your FIFO queue or provide an explicit `MessageDeduplicationId` parameter for each message. Here\'s an example of how to provide an explicit `MessageDeduplicationId` parameter using the `send_message` method in the Boto3 Python SDK:\n```python\nimport boto3\n\n# Set up the SQS client\nsqs = boto3.client(\'sqs\', aws_access_key_id=\'YOUR_ACCESS_KEY\',\n                   aws_secret_access_key=\'YOUR_SECRET_KEY\',\n                   region_name=\'YOUR_REGION\')\n\n# Send a message to the FIFO queue\nqueue_url = \'https://sqs.YOUR_REGION.amazonaws.com/YOUR_ACCOUNT/YOUR_QUEUE.fifo\'\nmessage = \'Hello, world!\'\nmessage_deduplication_id = \'some-unique-id\'\nresponse = sqs.send_message(QueueUrl=queue_url, MessageBody=message,\n                            MessageGroupId=\'1\', MessageDeduplicationId=message_deduplication_id)\n\nprint(f\'Sent message to {queue_url} with message ID {response["MessageId"]}\')\n```\nIn this example, `YOUR_QUEUE` is assumed to be the name of a FIFO queue (which has the suffix `.fifo` in its URL) that requires an explicit `MessageDeduplicationId` parameter. The `MessageDeduplicationId` value must be unique within the group of messages with the same `MessageGroupId`. If you try to send a message with a `MessageDeduplicationId` that was used within the last 5 minutes, the `SendMessage` API operation will fail with an error.\n\nNote that enabling Content-Based Deduplication is recommended when possible, as it simplifies message sending and avoids the need to generate and manage unique `MessageDeduplicationId` values. To enable Content-Based Deduplication, you can use the `CreateQueue` API operation or the SQS console to create a FIFO queue with the `ContentBasedDeduplication` attribute set to `true`. Once enabled, SQS automatically deduplicates messages based on their content.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [1986, 1465, 13666, 1576, 279, 1565, 80863, 63, 5333, 5666, 7460, 2987, 8883, 60339, 50399, 454, 1693, 476, 458, 11464, 1565, 2052, 35, 291, 454, 1693, 764, 63, 5733, 979, 11628, 6605, 311, 264, 47007, 320, 5338, 31500, 12, 5338, 84515, 8, 7177, 13, 47007, 48094, 525, 6188, 311, 21129, 279, 1973, 315, 6605, 323, 1824, 1943, 5203, 11, 892, 525, 44792, 315, 6605, 429, 9173, 311, 279, 1852, 11457, 1874, 382, 2679, 8883, 60339, 50399, 454, 1693, 374, 8970, 11, 279, 1849, 9463, 7681, 40614, 6605, 3118, 389, 862, 2213, 13, 18214, 11, 498, 1969, 3410, 458, 11464, 1565, 2052, 35, 291, 454, 1693, 764, 63, 5733, 429, 35511, 279, 1943, 323, 20081, 7681, 454, 1693, 382, 1249, 5046, 419, 1465, 11, 498, 646, 2987, 7283, 8883, 60339, 50399, 454, 1693, 369, 697, 47007, 7177, 476, 3410, 458, 11464, 1565, 2052, 35, 291, 454, 1693, 764, 63, 5733, 369, 1817, 1943, 13, 5692, 594, 458, 3110, 315, 1246, 311, 3410, 458, 11464, 1565, 2052,