INFO 03-13 07:54:39 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-cddcc777d4f24d77b10fe1a032cd8717-0: prompt: "I apologize for the confusion in my previous response. It looks like the `WaitAsync()` method is not actually available on the `WaitHandle` class.\n\nInstead, you can use the `WaitOneAsync()` extension method provided by the `System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions` namespace. This method is available in .NET 6 and later versions, and allows you to wait for a `WaitHandle` asynchronously.\n\nHere's the updated version of the code using `WaitOneAsync()`:\n```csharp\nusing System;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing DSharpPlus;\nusing DSharpPlus.Entities;\nusing DSharpPlus.EventArgs;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions;\n\npublic async Task ListenForMessageUpdates(DiscordClient client)\n{\n    var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(60));\n    \n    client.MessageUpdated += ClientOnMessageUpdated;\n\n    await cts.Token.WaitHandle.WaitOneAsync();\n    \n    client.MessageUpdated -= ClientOnMessageUpdated;\n\n    cts.Dispose();\n}\n\nprivate Task ClientOnMessageUpdated(DiscordClient client, MessageUpdateEventArgs e)\n{\n    Console.WriteLine(e.MessageBefore.Content);\n    Console.WriteLine(e.Message.Content);\n    \n    return Task.CompletedTask;\n}\n```\nIn this version of the code, the `WaitOneAsync()` method is called on the `WaitHandle` property of the cancellation token's `Token` property. This returns a `Task<bool>` object that represents the asynchronous wait operation.\n\nThe `System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions` namespace provides an extension method that allows you to await this task directly, using the `await` keyword.\n\nMake sure you have the appropriate using directive for `System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions` in your code, as shown in the example above.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[