INFO 03-13 07:54:40 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-cd565988f4fc4d4899a71a4846475f45-0: prompt: 'Sure, here are some materials and examples that could be used to teach students how to participate in a group chat:\n\n* Examples of good and bad participation in a group chat:\n\t+ Good: "Hi everyone, I just wanted to let you know that I finished Task 3 of the project and I\'m ready to move on to Task 4. Can anyone provide an update on their progress and when we can expect to meet again?"\n\t+ Bad: "Ugh, I\'m so behind on this project. I don\'t know how I\'m going to finish everything in time."\n* Handouts or worksheets on how to participate in a group chat:\n\t+ Tips for writing clear and concise messages\n\t+ Examples of how to provide updates and ask for help\n\t+ Guidance on how to respond to others\' messages and contribute to the conversation\n* Exercises or activities to practice participating in a group chat:\n\t+ Students could be given a scenario and asked to write a message for a group chat\n\t+ Students could participate in a simulated group chat, where they practice sending and responding to messages\n\t+ Students could participate in a real group chat, with guidance and feedback from the instructor\n\nOverall, the goal of these materials would be to help students learn how to participate in a group chat in a way that is clear, concise, and respectful. By providing examples, guidance, and practice opportunities, you can help students develop the skills they need to effectively communicate in a group chat.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [3981