INFO 03-13 07:54:40 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-18e8b201260e4cd5aa0988ff9b18104c-0: prompt: 'If you want to put your controller behind an API Gateway, you need to configure your application to work with the API Gateway. Here are some steps you can take to do this:\n\n1. Configure HTTPS: You should use HTTPS for all communication between the API Gateway and your application. You can configure HTTPS in the `ConfigureWebHostDefaults` method of the `Program` class by adding the `UseHttps` method:\n```csharp\npublic static void Main(string[] args)\n{\n    CreateHostBuilder(args).Build().Run();\n}\n\npublic static IHostBuilder CreateHostBuilder(string[] args) =>\n    Host.CreateDefaultBuilder(args)\n        .ConfigureWebHostDefaults(webBuilder =>\n        {\n            webBuilder.UseStartup<Startup>()\n                .UseUrls("https://localhost:5001")\n                .UseHttps();\n        });\n```\nIn this example, we\'re configuring the application to use HTTPS with a self-signed certificate.\n2. Configure the API Gateway: You need to configure your API Gateway to forward requests to your application. This involves specifying the hostname and port of your application and the path to your controller. The exact steps for configuring the API Gateway will depend on the specific gateway you are using.\n3. Configure routing: If you are using an API Gateway that modifies the path of incoming requests (e.g. by adding a prefix), you may need to configure your application to handle the modified path. You can do this by configuring routing in the `Configure` method of the `Startup` class:\n```csharp\npublic void Configure(IApplicationBuilder app, IWebHostEnvironment env)\n{\n    // ...\n\n    app.UseRouting();\n\n    app.UseEndpoints(endpoints =>\n    {\n        endpoints.MapControllerRoute(\n            name: "default",\n            pattern: "{controller}/{action}/{id?}");\n    });\n}\n```\nIn this example, we\'re configuring the application to handle requests with a path that includes the name of the controller.\n\nBy default, ASP.NET Core applications listen on `localhost` and are not accessible from outside the host machine. To make your application accessible from the API Gateway, you need to listen on a publicly accessible IP address and configure your firewall to allow traffic to that address. You should also configure authentication and authorization to secure your application.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2679, 498, 1366, 311, 2182, 697, 6461, 4815, 458, 5333, 39378, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 14411, 697, 3766, 311, 975, 448, 279, 5333, 39378, 13, 5692, 525, 1045, 7354, 498, 646, 1896, 311, 653, 419, 1447, 16, 13, 22169, 61044, 25, 1446, 1265, 990, 61044, 369, 678, 10535, 1948, 279, 5333, 39378, 323, 697, 3766, 13, 1446, 646, 14411, 61044, 304, 279, 1565, 28560, 89575, 16273, 63, 1714, 315, 279, 1565, 10690, 63, 536, 553, 7842, 279, 1565, 10253, 92869, 63, 1714, 510, 73594, 66, 52917, 198, 888, 1099, 737, 4697, 3609, 1294, 2827, 340, 515, 262, 4230, 9296, 3297, 7356, 568, 11066, 1005, 6727, 543, 630, 888, 1099, 358, 9296, 3297, 4230, 9296, 3297, 3609, 1294, 2827, 8, 6274, 262, 16102, 7251, 3675, 3297, 7356, 340, 286, 659, 28560, 89575, 16273, 39769, 3297, 6274, 286, 341, 310, 3482, 3297, 9046, 39076, 27, 39076, 18949, 394, 659, 10253, 15638, 445, 2428, 1110, 8301, 25, 20, 15, 15, 16, 1138, 394, 659, 10253, 92869, 543, 286, 1625, 13874, 3989, 641, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 2299, 71783, 279, 3766, 311, 990, 61044, 448, 264, 656, 92553, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 22169, 279, 5333, 39378, 25, 1446, 1184, 311, 14411, 697, 5333, 3937