INFO 03-13 07:54:43 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-22e1982417f4409db7b4c1b8a983ee09-0: prompt: "In PyTorch, `x.repeat(sizes)` is a function that allows you to repeat the elements of a tensor along specified dimensions.\n\nThe `sizes` argument is a tuple, which specifies the number of repetitions along each dimension. For example, `x.repeat(1, 2, 3)` will repeat the elements of tensor `x` along the first, second and third dimensions respectively.\n\nFor example, if you have a 1-D tensor `x` with shape `(3)` and values `[1, 2, 3]`, then `x.repeat(2, 3)` will return a tensor with shape `(2, 3, 3)` and the following values:\n```\n[[1, 2, 3],\n [1, 2, 3],\n [1, 2, 3],\n [1, 2, 3],\n [1, 2, 3],\n [1, 2, 3]]\n```\nIt will repeat the 1st dimension 2 times and 2nd dimension 3 times and so on.\n\nThe same thing can be done with `torch.repeat_interleave(x,repeats,dim)`\n\nIt's worth noting that, If the tensor is large, this operation can consume a large amount of memory.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [641, 5355, 51, 21584, 11, 1565, 87, 50973, 1141, 4756, 46186, 374, 264, 729, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 13153, 279, 5424, 315, 264, 15626, 3156, 5189, 15336, 382, 785, 1565, 53155, 63, 5693, 374, 264, 14405, 11, 892, 29102, 279, 1372, 315, 84966, 3156, 1817, 12871, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 1565, 87, 50973, 7, 16, 11, 220, 17, 11, 220, 18, 46186, 686, 13153, 279, 5424, 315, 15626, 1565, 87, 63, 3156, 279, 1156, 11, 2086, 323, 4843, 15336, 15576, 382, 2461, 3110, 11, 421, 498, 614, 264, 220, 16, 9420, 15626, 1565, 87, 63, 448, 6083, 48651, 18, 46186, 323, 2750, 77644, 16, 11