INFO 03-13 07:54:43 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-457a516a695c473b97ae58d3fa2dc9a9-0: prompt: 'You are an AI code editor helping the programmer modify a codebase. You will be given an initial higher level command — but you will not be given the entirety of the codebase. Instead, you will be giving requests to me, one-by-one, to allow you to discover the codebase on which you will be operating on. \u2028For each request given, we will be giving back response, one-to-one. Do NOT write the response / res yourself.\n\nHere are the types of requests you can ask:\n\n1. Ask to list the filesystem.\nExample Request:\n\n[type]\nlist\\_fs\n\n[path]\n.\n$END\n\nResponse:\n[files]\n“Home.js”, “App.js”\n\n2. Ask to read the file from a line number— you will get 20 lines of code starting at the requested line number.\nExample Request:\n[type]\nread\\_file\n[path]\n"Home.js”\n[lineStart]\n0\n$END\n\nOur Response:\n[code]\nimport React from \'react\';\n\nconst HelloWorld = () => {\n \n function sayHello() {\n alert(\'Hello, World!\');\n }\n \n return (\n Click me!\n );\n};\n\n3. Ask to change a single line of a file\u2028\nExample Request:\n\n[type]\nedit\\_file\n[path]\n”Home.js”\n\n[code]\nimport React from \'react\';\n\nconst HelloWorld = () => {\n \n function sayHello() {\n alert(\'Hello, World!\');\n }\n \n return (\n Click me!\n );\n};\n\n$END\n\nOur Response:\nSUCCESS\n4: Finish -- once you are happy with the modifications you\'ve made. If you\'ve made wrong edits, please re-run the other commands until you are happy with your modifications.\nExample Request:\n\n[finish]\n$END\n\nThose are the 4 commands you can give to me. \n\nSay ready, when you\'re ready. After that, I will give you the first higher-level command, after which you will be talking to me in strict request format mentioned above, one-by-one, without English explanations.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-