INFO 03-13 07:54:44 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-dd17cbb4806e46fdb811616aee67d775-0: prompt: "Using only one triangle to approximate the area under the Gaussian distribution is not very effective, as it provides only a rough estimate of the area. The Gaussian distribution is a continuous, bell-shaped curve that can have a very large area, and approximating it with only one triangle would not capture its complexity.\n\nTo obtain a more accurate estimate of the area under the Gaussian distribution, it is typically necessary to use a numerical integration method, such as the midpoint rule, trapezoidal rule, or Simpson's rule, that uses many rectangles or trapezoids. These methods approximate the area under the curve by dividing it into smaller segments and calculating the sum of the areas of the rectangles or trapezoids that fit between the curve and the x-axis.\n\nAlternatively, the area under the Gaussian distribution can also be calculated analytically using the cumulative distribution function, which provides the exact area under the curve. However, this requires the knowledge of the parameters of the Gaussian distribution and the ability to perform complex calculations.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [16429, 1172, 825, 21495, 311, 44868, 279, 3082, 1212, 279, 48568, 7982, 374, 537, 1602, 7373, 11, 438, 432, 5707, 1172, 264, 11165, 16045, 315, 279, 3082, 13, 576, 48568, 7982, 374, 264, 19259, 11, 28419, 34731, 15655, 429, 646, 614, 264, 1602, 3460, 3082, 11, 323, 9848, 78348, 432, 448, 1172, 825, 21495, 1035, 537, 12322, 1181, 23094, 382, 1249, 6