INFO 03-13 07:54:50 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-4e5d1c3bce534d03b7ba3e218a902c11-0: prompt: 'Macaque cautiously approached the magic barrier, holding a small bag of food in his hand. He looked around, searching for any sign of MK, but saw nothing.\n\n"MK?" Macaque called out softly, but there was no response.\n\nHe tried again, a little louder this time, "MK, can you hear me?"\n\nStill, there was no response. Macaque furrowed his brow in confusion and tried to look for any clues that might help him understand what was happening.\n\nAs he looked around, he noticed something strange. There were no footprints in the dirt leading up to the barrier. It was as if MK had disappeared into thin air.\n\nMacaque\'s confusion turned to worry. He knew something was wrong, but he didn\'t know what. He approached the barrier and pressed his hand against it, hoping to feel something on the other side.\n\nBut there was nothing.\n\nMacaque\'s heart sank. He knew that Wukong was a powerful magician, but he didn\'t realize that he was capable of this level of magic. He knew that he needed to find a way to break the spell and save MK, but he didn\'t know how.\n\n"Macaque?" a voice whispered in his ear.\n\nMacaque jumped and spun around, but there was no one there. He frowned, wondering if he was just imagining things.\n\nThen he heard it again, the same whisper, "Macaque, it\'s me, MK. Wukong cast a spell on me. I\'m invisible, but you can hear me because I\'m inside the barrier."\n\nMacaque\'s eyes widened in shock. He had never heard of a spell like that before. He pressed his hand against the barrier again, hoping to somehow reach MK.\n\n"I\'m here, MK. Don\'t worry, I\'ll figure something out. I won\'t leave you here," Macaque promised, his voice full of determination.\n\nMK sighed in relief. He knew he could count on Macaque to help him, even in the face of such powerful magic.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0