INFO 03-13 07:54:52 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-330829f4b7b248068bc095dd2c20a5ff-0: prompt: 'Understood, let\'s try a different approach to their dialogue.\n\n---\n\nSarah was at the edge of a tall building, staring down into the abyss below. She was feeling reckless, her mind consumed with the fantasies of death and what it would be like to let go. Suddenly, she heard a voice behind her, gentle and timid, but firm.\n\nWorm: "Oh, what a beautiful day it is to be alive. Don\'t you think so, Sarah?"\n\nSarah turned to see a man standing a few feet away from her. He was dressed in ragged clothes, but there was a twinkle in his eye that suggested he knew something that others didn\'t.\n\nSarah: "Who are you? And how do you know my name?"\n\nWorm: "Oh, I know all sorts of things. But I\'d much rather talk about the world. Have you seen the colors of the sky today? It\'s like a painting, isn\'t it?"\n\nSarah was taken aback. She wasn\'t used to being talked to like this. But something about this man was different, and she couldn\'t help but be drawn to him.\n\nSarah: "Yes, it is. But what does that have to do with anything?"\n\nWorm: "Everything! The sky is full of promise, and so is the world. There\'s so much to see and do. And you, Sarah, you\'re meant to be a part of it. Just imagine all the adventures you could have."\n\nSarah: "But I don\'t belong here. I feel like I don\'t fit in."\n\nWorm: "Nonsense! You fit in just fine. Just like you fit in the labyrinth, the place where you truly belong. Don\'t you remember all the wonders you saw there?"\n\nSarah: "The labyrinth? How do you know about that?"\n\nWorm: "I know all sorts of things. And I can take you there, if you\'d like. Just imagine, Sarah, all the wonders that await you."\n\nSarah: "Really? You can take me there?"\n\nWorm: "Of course. But first, let\'s go for a walk. There\'s so much to see and experience in this world. And who knows, we may even find our way to the labyrinth."\n\nSarah was hesitant, but the man\'s words filled her with a sense of hope. She decided to take a chance, and followed him as he led her away from the edge of the building and into the bustling city. The man\'s juggling of ideas and distractions proved effective, as Sarah was no longer consumed with thoughts of death and the abyss below.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [16250, 51684, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 264, 2155, 5486, 311, 862, 21276, 382, 44364, 53083, 572, 518, 279, 6821, 315, 264, 16217, 4752, 11, 36774, 1495, 1119, 279, 87214, 3685, 13, 2932, 572, 8266, 53217, 11, 1059, 3971, 25983, 448, 279, 59177, 315, 4545, 323, 1128, 432, 1035, 387, 1075, 311, 1077, 728, 13, 57701, 11, 1340, 6617, 264, 7743, 4815, 1059, 11, 21700, 323, 98049, 11, 714, 7474, 382, 54, 493, 25, 330, 11908, 11, 1128, 264, 6233, 1899, 432, 374, 311, 387, 13675, 13, 4320, 944, 498, 1744, 773, 11, 20445, 11974, 53083, 6519, 311, 1490, 264, 883, 11259, 264, 2421, 7541, 3123, 504, 1059, 13, 1260, 572, 25365, 304, 20475, 3556, 15097, 11, 714, 1052, 572, 264, 4384, 35144, 304, 806, 7912, 429, 11827, 566, 6876, 2494, 429, 3800, 3207, 944, 382, 53083, 25, 330, 15191, 525, 498, 30, 1597, 1246, 653, 498, 1414, 847, 829, 11974, 54, 493, 25, 330, 11908, 11, 358, 1414, 678, 20853, 315, 2513, 13, 1988, 358, 4172, 1753, 4751, 3061, 911, 279, 1879, 13, 12243, 498, 3884, 279, 7987, 315, 279, 12884, 3351, 30, 1084, 594, 1075, 264, 18824, 11, 4436, 944, 432, 11974, 53083, 572, 4429, 668, 473, 13, 2932, 5710, 944, 1483, 311, 1660, 14897, 311, 1075, 419, 13, 1988, 2494, 911, 419, 883, 572, 2155, 11, 323, 1340, 7691, 944, 149