INFO 03-13 07:54:54 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-54683d59d3504dc5b1cba817ac1a70a1-0: prompt: 'To put the SQL query to retrieve the station name into a PHP script that uses prepared statements and outputs the result as JSON, you can use the following code:\n```\n<?php\n\n// Connect to the database\n$host = "localhost";\n$user = "username";\n$password = "password";\n$dbname = "database_name";\n\n$conn = mysqli_connect($host, $user, $password, $dbname);\n\nif (!$conn) {\n  die("Connection failed: " . mysqli_connect_error());\n}\n\n// Set up the prepared statement\n$query = "SELECT name FROM Stations WHERE id = ?";\n\n$stmt = mysqli_prepare($conn, $query);\n\n// Bind the parameter\n$station_id = 2;\nmysqli_stmt_bind_param($stmt, "i", $station_id);\n\n// Execute the prepared statement\nmysqli_stmt_execute($stmt);\n\n// Bind the result\nmysqli_stmt_bind_result($stmt, $name);\n\n// Check for errors\nif (mysqli_stmt_error($stmt)) {\n  die("Prepared statement failed: " . mysqli_stmt_error($stmt));\n}\n\n// Fetch the result\nif (mysqli_stmt_fetch($stmt)) {\n  $result = array("name" => $name);\n} else {\n  $result = array("name" => null);\n}\n\n// Close the prepared statement and connection\nmysqli_stmt_close($stmt);\nmysqli_close($conn);\n\n// Output the result as JSON\necho json_encode($result);\n\n?>\n```\nThis script establishes a connection to the database using the `mysqli_connect` function, then sets up the prepared statement using the `mysqli_prepare` function. It binds the parameter using the `mysqli_stmt_bind_param` function and executes the prepared statement using the `mysqli_stmt_execute` function. It binds the result using the `mysqli_stmt_bind_result` function, checks for errors using the `mysqli_stmt_error` function, and fetches the result using the `mysqli_stmt_fetch` function.\n\nIf the query is successful and returns a result, it stores the name in the `$result` array. If the query returns no results', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0,