INFO 03-13 07:54:56 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-6f583b12d7e84b089fa8ffaf00e8cbd7-0: prompt: "Sure! Here's an example code for object detection with a CNN using Keras and TensorFlow:\n```python\n# Import required libraries\nimport tensorflow as tf\nfrom tensorflow import keras\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Load and preprocess the dataset\n(train_images, train_boxes), (test_images, test_boxes) = keras.datasets.cifar10.load_data()\n\n# Normalize images\ntrain_images = train_images / 255.0\ntest_images = test_images / 255.0\n\n# Convert bounding boxes to one-hot encoding\nnum_classes = 10\ntrain_boxes = keras.utils.to_categorical(train_boxes, num_classes)\ntest_boxes = keras.utils.to_categorical(test_boxes, num_classes)\n\n# Define the CNN model for object detection\nmodel = keras.Sequential([\n    keras.layers.Conv2D(32, (3,3), activation='relu', input_shape=(32,32,3)),\n    keras.layers.MaxPooling2D((2,2)),\n    keras.layers.Conv2D(64, (3,3), activation='relu'),\n    keras.layers.MaxPooling2D((2,2)),\n    keras.layers.Conv2D(64, (3,3), activation='relu'),\n    keras.layers.Flatten(),\n    keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu'),\n    keras.layers.Dense(num_classes * 4, activation='linear'),\n    keras.layers.Reshape((num_classes, 4))\n])\n\n# Compile the model\nmodel.compile(optimizer='adam',\n              loss='mse')\n\n# Train the model\nmodel.fit(train_images, train_boxes, epochs=10)\n\n# Evaluate the model on test data\ntest_loss = model.evaluate(test_images, test_boxes)\nprint('Test loss:', test_loss)\n\n# Use the model to detect objects in new data\npredictions = model.predict(test_images)\n\n# Calculate IOU (Intersection over Union) for the predicted boxes\nious = []\nfor i in range(len(predictions)):\n    pred_box = predictions[i]\n    true_box = test_boxes[i]\n    pred_coords = [pred_box[j] for j in range(4)]\n    true_coords = [true_box[j] for j in range(4)]\n    pred_left, pred_top, pred_right, pred_bottom = pred_coords\n    true_left, true_top, true_right, true_bottom = true_coords\n    x1 = max(pred_left, true_left)\n    y1 = max(pred_top, true_top)\n    x2 = min(pred_right, true_right)\n    y2 = min(pred_bottom, true_bottom)\n    intersection_area = max(x2 - x1, 0) * max(y2 - y1, 0)\n    pred_area = (pred_right - pred_left) * (pred_bottom - pred_top)\n    true_area = (true_right - true_left) * (true_bottom - true_top)\n    union_area = pred_area + true_area - intersection_area\n    iou = intersection_area / union_area\n    ious.append(iou)\n\n# Calculate mean IOU for all predictions\nmean_iou = np.mean(ious)\nprint('Mean IOU:', mean_iou)\n```\nThis code loads and preprocesses the CIFAR-10 dataset, defines a CNN model with appropriate layers for object detection, compiles the model with a mean squared error loss function, trains the model on the training data, evaluates the model on the test data, uses the model to detect objects in new data, and calculates the mean IOU for the predicted bounding boxes.\n\nNote that this is just an example, and depending on the specific dataset and problem you are working with, you may need to modify the code accordingly.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 0, 5692, 594, 458, 3110, 2038, 369, 1633, 17984, 448, 264, 19769, 1667, 730, 9247, 323, 94986, 510, 73594, 12669, 198, 2, 13213, 2567, 20186, 198, 474, 28087, 438, 6409, 198, 1499, 28087, 1159, 25689, 198, 474, 8591, 438, 2595, 271, 2, 8893, 323, 53465, 279, 10337, 198, 20307, 13283, 11, 5426, 38384, 701, 320, 1944, 13283, 11, 1273, 38384, 8, 284, 25689, 58152, 520, 92927, 16, 15, 5104, 1769, 2822, 2, 68092, 