INFO 03-13 07:54:59 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-333d97dbc17f4704aafe7603fbb9d45a-0: prompt: 'To address scalability challenges in a cloud-based solution, one could utilize several services in Amazon Web Services (AWS) such as:\n\n1. Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2): provides scalable computing capacity in the cloud, allowing you to quickly scale your application as demand grows.\n2. Amazon Auto Scaling: automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances to handle changes in demand.\n3. Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS): provides a managed message queue service that enables decoupling of the components of a cloud application.\n4. Amazon ElastiCache: provides in-memory caching that can be used to offload read-intensive database workloads, which can improve the performance and scalability of your application.\n5. Amazon DynamoDB: a fast, fully managed NoSQL database that can automatically scale and handle large amounts of data and traffic.\n6. Amazon S3: provides scalable and durable object storage, which can be used to store large amounts of data, media, and backups.\n\nThese AWS services can be used together to build a scalable and highly available cloud-based solution that can handle increasing demand while maintaining high performance.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [1249, 2621, 93740, 11513, 304, 264, 9437, 5980, 6291, 11, 825, 1410, 28066, 3807, 3516, 304, 8176, 4895, 8307, 320, 36136, 8, 1741, 438, 1447, 16, 13, 8176, 51910, 22603, 14817, 320, 7498, 17, 1648, 5707, 68211, 24231, 8654, 304, 279, 9437, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 6157, 5452, 697, 376