INFO 03-13 07:54:59 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-02f404ae7c6f4d02a9227393c1571d87-0: prompt: "Sure, here's a comparison of the international web traffic, engagement metrics, and KPIs for ProQuest and its top 10 competitors:\n\n| Platform | Year Launched | Market Share | Engagement Metrics | Target Audience | International Web Traffic (SimilarWeb) | Monthly Visits (SimilarWeb) | Monthly Pageviews (SimilarWeb) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ProQuest | 1938 | 25% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 15,900,000 | 18.3M | 104M |\n| JSTOR | 1995 | 10% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 5,800,000 | 6.9M | 50M |\n| EBSCO | 1944 | 10% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 7,800,000 | 9.8M | 61M |\n| Google Scholar | 2004 | 8% | Searches, downloads | Researchers, students, and librarians | 8,200,000,000 | 188M | 4.4B |\n| Scopus | 2004 | 5% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 2,200,000 | 2.5M | 19M |\n| Web of Science | 1964 | 5% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 2,100,000 | 2.7M | 18M |\n| Project MUSE | 1993 | 3% | Searches, downloads | Researchers, students, and librarians | 675,000 | 790K | 6.2M |\n| Ovid | 1988 | 2% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 285,000 | 320K | 2.6M |\n| SpringerLink | 1997 | 2% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 2,800,000 | 3.2M | 25M |\n| Taylor & Francis Online | 1997 | 2% | Searches, downloads, user feedback | Researchers, students, and librarians | 5,800,000 | 6.4M | 53M |\n\nNote: Data is current as of March 2023 and may be subject to change.\n\nAs we can see from the table, ProQuest has the highest international web traffic with over 15 million monthly visits, followed by JSTOR with over 6.9 million monthly visit