INFO 03-13 07:55:01 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-23a504774ec342da911c0a95ca0979a9-0: prompt: 'Here are some best practices for sourcing Indonesian suppliers using the Indonesia-Australia Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (IA-CEPA):\n\n1. Research potential suppliers: Start by researching potential suppliers in Indonesia that offer the products or services you need. Look for suppliers that have a good reputation, are reliable, and offer competitive prices.\n2. Evaluate supplier capabilities: Carefully evaluate the capabilities of potential suppliers to ensure that they can meet your quality, delivery, and other requirements. Look for suppliers that have the capacity to handle your order volume and are able to produce products to your specifications.\n3. Establish clear terms and conditions: Clearly define the terms and conditions of your business relationship with your supplier, including delivery schedules, payment terms, and any other important details. This will help ensure that you are both on the same page and avoid misunderstandings down the line.\n4. Negotiate favorable terms: Use IA-CEPA to negotiate favorable terms with your supplier, including price, delivery schedules, and any other key terms. IA-CEPA can provide benefits in terms of reduced tariffs and improved market access, which can potentially help you secure better terms with your supplier.\n5. Monitor supplier performance: Regularly monitor the performance of your supplier to ensure that they are meeting your expectations and delivering on their commitments. Use this information to identify any potential issues and work with your supplier to resolve them.\n\nBy following these best practices, you can build a strong, mutually beneficial relationship with your Indonesian supplier and use IA-CEPA to your advantage. Remember to carefully research and evaluate potential suppliers, and seek the guidance of a business advisor or mentor if needed.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_pen