INFO 03-13 07:55:03 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-8b8d779c3728483993df0ac91d36c048-0: prompt: "Both GStreamer and FFmpeg are popular multimedia frameworks that provide similar functionality, but they have different design philosophies and strengths.\n\nGStreamer is a modular framework for building multimedia applications that provides a pipeline-based architecture for processing and transforming audio and video streams. It is written in C and has bindings for several other languages, including Python, Java, and Rust. GStreamer's modularity and extensibility make it well-suited for complex multimedia applications that require advanced processing and transformation capabilities. GStreamer also has a strong focus on support for open standards and interoperability with other multimedia frameworks.\n\nFFmpeg, on the other hand, is primarily a command-line tool for transcoding and processing audio and video files, but it can also be used as a library for building multimedia applications. It is written in C and has bindings for several other languages. FFmpeg's strength lies in its broad support for a wide range of audio and video codecs and formats, making it a versatile tool for handling multimedia files. FFmpeg is also widely used in the multimedia industry and has a large and active user community.\n\nIn terms of weaknesses, some users find GStreamer's modular architecture and complex API challenging to work with, while others find FFmpeg's command-line interface to be less user-friendly than other multimedia tools. Additionally, because GStreamer is designed to be extensible, its performance may not be as optimized as more specialized multimedia frameworks. Conversely, because FFmpeg is primarily a command-line tool, it may not provide the same level of modularity and extensibility as more framework-oriented solutions.\n\nUltimately, the choice between GStreamer and FFmpeg will depend on the specific requirements of the application and the preferences of the developer or team.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [20629, 479, 80063, 323, 29942, 47551, 525, 5411, 56513, 48025, 429, 3410, 4428, 14944, 11, 714, 807, 614, 2155, 2884, 13556, 550, 323, 35386, 382, 38, 80063, 374, 264, 43893, 12626, 369, 4752, 56513, 8357, 429, 5707, 264, 15301, 5980, 17646, 369, 8692, 323, 45790, 7699, 323, 2766, 23045, 13, 1084, 374, 5326, 304, 356, 323, 702, 35700, 369, 3807, 1008, 15459, 11, 2670, 13027, 11, 7943, 11, 323, 33789, 13, 479, 80063, 594, 1463, 28979, 323, 1303, 724, 3147, 1281, 432, 1632, 86129, 1608, 369, 6351, 56513, 8357, 429, 1373, 10847, 8692, 323, 17991, 16928, 13, 479, 80063, 1083, 702, 264, 3746, 5244, 389, 1824, 369, 1787, 10659, 323, 94130, 2897, 448, 1008, 56513, 48025, 382, 1748, 47551, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 374, 15503, 264, 3210, 8447, 5392, 369, 41490, 3700, 323, 8692, 7699, 323, 2766, 3542, 11, 714, 432, 646, 1083, 387, 1483, 438, 264, 6733, 369, 4752, 56513, 8357, 13, 1084, 374, 5326, 304, 356, 323, 702, 35700, 369, 3807, 1008, 15459, 13, 29942, 47551, 594, 8170, 15448, 304, 1181, 7205, 1824, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 7699, 323, 2766, 56152, 323, 19856, 11, 3259, 432, 264, 31945, 5392, 369, 11589, 56513, 3542, 13, 29942, 47551, 374, 1083, 13570, 1483, 304, 279, 56513, 4958, 323, 702, 264, 3460, 323, 4541, 1196, 3942, 382, 641, 3793, 315, 43567, 11, 1045, 3847, 1477, 479, 80063, 594, 43893, 17646, 323, 6351, 5333, 17003, 311, 975, 448, 11, 1393, 3800, 1477, 29942, 47551, 594, 3210, 8447, 3749, 311, 387, 2686, 1196, 21896, 1091, 1008, 56513, 7375, 13, 22406, 11, 1576, 479, 80063, 374, 6188, 311, 387, 