d threatens to take legal action if Jack and his family do not agree to the recommended treatment plan. They bring in hospital lawyers to try to convince Jack to change his mind, but he remains firm in his belief that the blood transfusions are not in line with his family's religious beliefs.\n* The situation becomes even more complicated when Sarah's cancer spreads to her bone marrow, and she becomes dependent on blood transfusions to survive. Jack and his family are torn between their religious beliefs and their love for Sarah, and they struggle to make a decision.\n* In the final scene of the novel, Sarah dies peacefully in her hospital bed, surrounded by her family and Mike. Jack is heartbroken, but he takes comfort in the fact that they did everything they could to save her. As he reflects on the past year, he realizes that he has learned a lot about faith, family, and the importance of love. Despite the legal battles and the tensions within the family, Jack is grateful for the support and care that Sarah received from Mike and the other medical professionals at the hospital.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [95456, 13, 5692, 374, 264, 31728, 7089, 369, 264, 11514, 911, 264, 6981, 879, 4278, 438, 264, 8777, 84769, 323, 40616, 264, 6543, 19839, 7560, 369, 806, 9803, 11, 448, 3694, 19584, 15860, 8777, 21177, 1447, 9, 576, 3364, 12033, 448, 264, 21771, 6109, 304, 892, 279, 6981, 11, 7607, 11, 374, 37017, 806, 9803, 11, 20445, 11, 311, 279, 12851, 3054, 1283, 1340, 86358, 518, 2114, 13, 7607, 374, 264, 8777, 84769, 323, 374, 11285, 448, 279, 8777, 594, 29