INFO 03-13 07:55:09 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-e939a774064b4d87bd4f0f57bf6dd74b-0: prompt: 'Black box testing is a type of software testing that focuses on the external behavior of the software application without considering the internal logic or structure of the code. The goal of black box testing is to ensure that the software application meets the desired requirements and specifications, and performs as expected under a variety of different scenarios and conditions.\n\nOne common black box testing strategy is equivalence partitioning. Equivalence partitioning is a technique that involves dividing the input values for a software application into groups or partitions that are expected to behave in the same way. The idea behind this technique is to reduce the number of test cases required to adequately test the software application, while still ensuring that all possible scenarios are covered.\n\nThe steps involved in equivalence partitioning are as follows:\n\n1. Identify the input values for the software application that need to be tested.\n2. Divide the input values into groups or partitions based on their expected behavior. For example, if the input values are numeric, you might divide them into groups based on whether they are positive, negative, or zero.\n3. Select one representative value from each partition to use as a test case. For example, if you have three partitions (positive, negative, and zero), you might select one representative value from each partition (e.g. 5, -5, and 0) to use as test cases.\n4. Execute the test cases and compare the actual results to the expected results.\n5. Repeat the process with additional representative values from each partition as needed to ensure adequate test coverage.\n\nEquivalence partitioning is a powerful technique because it can help reduce the number of test cases required to achieve adequate test coverage, while still ensuring that all possible scenarios are covered. By dividing input values into groups based on their expected behavior, testers can focus on testing the most important scenarios, and can reduce the risk of missing critical defects or issues in the software application.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [14417, 3745, 7497, 374, 264, 943, 315, 3162, 7497, 429, 23497, 389, 279, 9250, 7709, 315, 279, 3162, 3766, 2041, 12831, 279, 5306, 12218, 476, 5944, 315, 279, 2038, 13, 576, 5795, 315, 3691, 3745, 7497, 374, 311, 5978, 429, 279, 3162, 3766, 20027, 279, 12685, 8502, 323, 28703, 11, 323, 26674, 438, 3601, 1212, 264, 8045, 315, 2155, 25283, 323, 4682, 382, 3966, 4185, 3691, 3745, 7497, 8282, 374, 84162, 16658, 287, 13, 11702, 88790, 16658, 287, 374, 264, 14762, 429, 17601, 49702, 279, 1946, 2750, 369, 264, 3162, 3766, 1119, 5203, 476, 46688, 429, 525, 3601, 311, 35692, 304, 279, 1852, 1616, 13, 576, 4522, 4815, 419, 14762, 374, 311, 7949, 279, 1372, 315, 1273, 5048, 2567, 311, 48572, 1273, 279, 3162, 3766, 11, 1393, 2058, 22573, 429, 678, 3204, 25283, 525, 9761, 382, 785, 7354, 6398, 304, 84162, 16658, 287, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1946, 2750, 369, 279, 3162, 3766, 429, 1184, 311, 387, 12510, 624, 17, 13, 62902, 279, 1946, 2750, 1119, 5203, 476, 46688, 3118, 389, 862, 3601, 7709, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 279, 1946, 2750, 525, 24064, 11, 498, 2578, 21749, 1105, 1119, 5203, 3118, 389, 3425, 807, 525, 6785, 11, 8225, 11, 476, 7168, 624, 18, 13, 8427, 825, 18239, 897, 504, 1817, 16658, 311, 990, 438, 264, 1273, 1142, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 498, 614, 2326, 46688, 320, 30487, 11, 8225, 11, 323, 7168, 701, 498, 2578, 3293, 825, 1