INFO 03-13 07:55:11 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-b7a401430d0444329c1b0d148de99564-0: prompt: 'Sure! Here\'s the complete Snakemake workflow using Postgres API to read sample information and GATK best practices to align and process the samples:\n```python\n# Define the input and output directories\ninput_dir = "input"\noutput_dir = "output"\ntmp_dir = "tmp"\n\n# Define the reference genome and known variant sites\nreference_genome = "ref/hg19.fa"\ndbsnp = "ref/dbsnp_138.hg19.vcf"\n\n# Define the config file\nconfigfile: "config.yaml"\n\n# Load the required Python modules\nimport pandas as pd\nimport psycopg2\n\n# Load the configuration file\nconfig = pd.read_csv(configfile, index_col=False)\n\n# Define the rule to generate the reference index\nrule index_reference:\n    input:\n        reference_genome\n    output:\n        reference_genome + ".fai"\n    shell:\n        "samtools faidx {input}"\n\n# Define the rule to generate the reference dictionary\nrule dict_reference:\n    input:\n        reference_genome\n    output:\n        reference_genome.rdict\n    shell:\n        "gatk CreateSequenceDictionary -R {input} -O {output}"\n\n# Define the rule to perform alignment of paired-end reads using BWA\nrule align:\n    input:\n        fastq1 = f"{input_dir}/{row.sample_id}_1.fastq",\n        fastq2 = f"{input_dir}/{row.sample_id}_2.fastq",\n        index = reference_genome,\n    output:\n        bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.bam"\n    params:\n        platform = row.platform,\n    shell:\n        "bwa mem -M -t 4 -R \'@RG\\\\tID:{row.sample_id}\\\\tSM:{row.sample_id}\\\\tPL:{params.platform}\' "\n        "{input.index} {input.fastq1} {input.fastq2} "\n        "| samtools view -Sb - > {output.bam}"\n\n# Define the rule to sort and index the BAM files\nrule sort_and_index:\n    input:\n        bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.bam",\n        reference = reference_genome,\n    output:\n        sorted_bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.sorted.bam"\n    shell:\n        "samtools sort -@ 4 -o {output.sorted_bam} -T {wildcards.sample_id}_tmp "\n        "{input.bam} && "\n        "samtools index {output.sorted_bam}"\n\n# Define the rule to mark duplicates using Picard\nrule mark_duplicates:\n    input:\n        bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.sorted.bam",\n    output:\n        marked_bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.dedup.bam",\n        metrics = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.dedup.metrics"\n    shell:\n        "gatk MarkDuplicates -I {input.bam} -O {output.marked_bam} -M {output.metrics} --CREATE_INDEX true --VALIDATION_STRINGENCY SILENT"\n\n# Define the rule to perform base quality score recalibration using GATK\nrule base_recalibration:\n    input:\n        bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.dedup.bam",\n        reference = reference_genome,\n        known_sites = dbsnp\n    output:\n        recalibrated_bam = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.recal.bam",\n        recalibration_report = f"{output_dir}/{row.sample_id}.recal_data.table"\n    shell:\n        "gatk BaseRecalibrator -R {input.reference} -I {input.bam} --known-sites {input.known_sites} "\n        "--output {output.recalibration_report}\n```', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 0, 5692, 594, 279, 4583, 13059, 585, 336, 726, 28288, 1667, 3877, 17818, 5333, 311, 1349, 6077, 1995, 323, 479, 828, 42, 1850, 12378, 311, 5285, 323, 1882, 279, 10469, 510, 73594, 12669, 198, 2, 18614, 279, 1946, 323, 2550, 28625, 198, 1355, 4334, 284, 330, 1355, 698, 3006, 4334, 284, 330, 3006, 698, 5173, 4334, 284, 330, 5173, 1837, 2, 18614, 279, 5785, 32769