INFO 03-13 07:55:12 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-c87b7c30124c405882f3c72a0c3e84e7-0: prompt: 'Sure, here\'s an example implementation for moving an entity with the arrow keys in Maplestory Worlds style Lua script:\n```lua\n--@ BeginEntityEventHandler\n--@ Scope=All\n--@ Target=service:InputService\n--@ EventName=KeyDownEvent\nfunction HandleKeyDownEvent(event)\n    -- Get the entity that this script is attached to\n    local entity = self.Entity\n    -- Get the PhysicsRigidbodyComponent of the entity\n    local rigidbody = entity.PhysicsRigidbodyComponent\n    \n    -- Check which key was pressed\n    if event.key == KeyboardKey.A then\n        -- Move entity to the left\n        rigidbody:AddForce(Vector2(-500, 0))\n    elseif event.key == KeyboardKey.D then\n        -- Move entity to the right\n        rigidbody:AddForce(Vector2(500, 0))\n    elseif event.key == KeyboardKey.W then\n        -- Move entity up\n        rigidbody:AddForce(Vector2(0, 500))\n    elseif event.key == KeyboardKey.S then\n        -- Move entity down\n        rigidbody:AddForce(Vector2(0, -500))\n    end\nend\n--@ EndEntityEventHandler\n```\nNote: I assumed that `KeyboardKey` is a predefined enum type in Maplestory Worlds, and I used `KeyboardKey.A`, `KeyboardKey.D`, `KeyboardKey.W`, `KeyboardKey.S` to represent the keys "A", "D", "W", "S" respectively. Please adjust the key codes accordingly if needed.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [39814, 11, 1588, 594, 458, 3110, 8129, 369, 7218, 458, 5387, 448, 279, 17921, 6894, 304, 43470, 26485, 51847, 1707, 37662, 5316, 510, 73594,