INFO 03-13 07:55:17 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-b70a06252e1a40d6864eff54d8a16108-0: prompt: "You can map the error returned from the Supabase client to your custom error by creating a new instance of your custom error class and passing the relevant information from the Supabase error as arguments to the constructor. Here's an example implementation:\n```typescript\nclass MyAppError extends Error {\n  status: number;\n  source: string;\n\n  constructor(status: number, message: string, source: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.status = status;\n    this.source = source;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function fetchData() {\n  const { data, error } = await supabase.from('mytable').select();\n\n  if (error) {\n    const myAppError = new MyAppError(error.status, error.message, 'Supabase');\n    handleCustomError(myAppError);\n    throw myAppError;\n  }\n\n  return data;\n}\n```\nIn the above example, if the Supabase client returns an error, we create a new instance of `MyAppError` and pass the relevant information from the Supabase error (`error.status`, `error.message`, and `'Supabase'` as the `source`). We then pass this custom error instance to our `handleCustomError` function, and finally throw the custom error so it can be caught and handled appropriately elsewhere in the code.", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [2610, 646, 2415, 279, 1465, 5927, 504, 279, 6299, 370, 519, 2943, 311, 697, 2526, 1465, 553, 6825, 264, 501, 2867, 315, 697, 2526, 1465, 536, 323, 12299, 279, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 6299, 370, 519, 1465, 438, 5977, 311, 279, 4692, 13, 5692, 594, 458