INFO 03-13 07:55:17 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-1c4f2357d6b8472ca31ace905469a7a9-0: prompt: 'What is a Livelihood Business Incubator (LBI) and what are its objectives and functions according to the revised operational guidelines? Who is eligible to submit a proposal and what is the institutional arrangement for LBIs?\n\nA Livelihood Business Incubator (LBI) is an entity that provides skill development and incubation programs to promote entrepreneurship and employment generation in the agro-rural sector, with a focus on rural and underserved areas. According to the revised operational guidelines, the objectives of an LBI are to generate employment opportunities, skill and upskill unemployed and existing self-employed/wage earners in new technologies, provide skilled human capital to nearby industrial clusters, and promote innovations for strengthening the competitiveness in the MSME sector.\n\nThe functions of an LBI include conducting outreach programs to create awareness about the initiative and onboard prospective beneficiaries, designing and conducting incubation programs for formal, scalable micro-enterprise creation, offering varied support services like financial, legal, product designing, accreditation, and compliance to existing & informal enterprises to formalize them and make them scalable, facilitating funding for micro-entrepreneurs, providing hands-on training to trainees, creating a conducive ecosystem for promoting entrepreneurship and generating employment, and making provision for using the facility at the Livelihood Business Incubation centre for development of product prototypes.\n\nAny agency/institution of Government of India/State government, existing training centres under Ministries/Departments of Government of India/State Government, industry associations, academic institutions, or any not-for-profit private institutions with experience in successfully executing incubation and/or skill development programs may be eligible to set up an LBI. The applicant organization should select a Mentor Institute and upload the proposal through the selected Mentor Institute as per the prescribed format online at [www.aspire.msme.gov.in](http://www.aspire.msme.gov.in). The institutional arrangement for LBIs includes a Scheme Steering Committee (SSC) and Mentor Institutes (MI). SSC will consider the proposals of the Host/Applicant Institutions for setting up of LBI, submitted through MI, and shall extend approval based on satisfying all the parameters set up by the SSC. MIs will assist and handhold the applicant/Host institutes & the LBIs in their day-to-day operations and act as a SPOC between the Ministry and the Host Institute/LBI. The detailed eligibility conditions & procedure for selection for Mentor Institutes has been enclosed as Annexure 2, and the performance of the MI will be monitored both on quantitative & qualitative aspects by the SSC.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [3838, 374, 264, 36211, 19906, 8025, 4848, 392, 850, 320, 43, 8598, 8, 323, 1128, 525, 1181, 25398, 323, 5746, 4092, 311, 279, 31728, 24586, 17501, 30, 10479, 374, 17013, 311, 9318, 264, 13734, 323, 1128, 374, 279, 32132, 26112, 369, 40150, 3872, 1939, 32, 36211, 19906, 8025, 4848, 392, 850, 320, 43, 8598, 8, 374, 458, 5387, 429, 5707, 9947, 4401, 323, 48627, 367, 7468, 311, 11926, 74405, 323, 14402, 9471, 304, 279, 933, 299, 3795, 4176, 10486, 11, 448, 264, 5244, 389, 19082, 323, 25373, 2771, 5671, 13, 10548, 311, 279, 31728, 24586, 17501, 11, 279, 25398, 315, 458, 444, 8598, 525, 311, 6923, 14402, 10488, 11, 9947, 323, 7