INFO 03-13 07:55:18 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-a282b499bd624c57ae86c7a08073abbd-0: prompt: "Here is the explanation of the translation process of Expedia:\n\n| Aspect | Explanation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Localization Strategy | Expedia uses a combination of centralization and localization strategies in their translation process. They have a centralized team that manages the translation process, but also have local teams to handle specific regions. |\n| Teams | Expedia has a dedicated localization team responsible for managing the translation process. They also work with external translation agencies for certain languages. |\n| TMS | Expedia uses a Translation Management System (TMS) to manage and automate their translation process. They use a customized version of SDL Trados for this purpose. |\n| MT | Machine Translation (MT) is used by Expedia to handle high-volume, low-priority content. They use custom MT engines developed in-house, as well as third-party MT providers. |\n| TM | Expedia uses Translation Memories (TM) to store previously translated content and reuse it when necessary. They have a large TM database that is used to ensure consistency and speed up the translation process. |\n| CMS Integration | Expedia integrates their translation process with their Content Management System (CMS) to ensure that translated content is seamlessly integrated into their website. |\n| Security | Expedia takes security seriously and ensures that all translation vendors and tools they work with are compliant with their security standards. |\n| Standards and Guidelines | Expedia has developed their own Translation Style Guide and Glossary to ensure consistency in terminology and tone across all translations. |\n| I18N tools | Expedia uses a variety of Internationalization (I18N) tools, including a language identifier tool and a character set detection tool. |\n| Methods | Expedia uses a combination of human translation, machine translation, and post-editing to ensure high-quality translations while also keeping costs and timeframes in check. |\n| Models | Expedia uses a combination of Statistical and Neural Machine Translation models for their MT engines. |\n| Workflows | Expedia has a well-defined translation workflow that includes several stages, including source text extraction, translation, quality assurance, and content integration. |\n| Customization | Expedia customizes their translation process to suit the specific needs of each region they operate in, including content type, tone, and style. |\n| Technics | Expedia uses a variety of translation technologies, including Translation Memory, Machine Translation, Translation Management System, and Content Management System, to ensure a streamlined translation process. |\n| Reporting and Analytics | Expedia uses analytics tools to track and monitor translation metrics, including translation volume, quality, and cost, to ensure that their translation process is efficient and effective. |\n| Vendors | Expedia works with a variety of external translation vendors to handle translations for certain languages. |\n| Reviews/LQA | Expedia has a dedicated Linguistic Quality Assurance (LQA) team responsible for reviewing and editing translations to ensure quality and accuracy. |\n| Scalability | Expedia's translation process is designed to be scalable, with the ability to handle large volumes of content and multiple languages simultaneously. |\n| User Friendliness | Expedia's translation process is designed to be user-friendly, with a simple interface that makes it easy for translators to work efficiently. |\n| Cost | Expedia's translation costs are carefully managed to ensure that they are cost-effective and scalable. |\n| User/License Limits | Expedia has a system in place to manage user and license limits for their translation tools and systems. |\n| Collaboration | Expedia fosters collaboration between their localization team, translation vendors, and other stakeholders to ensure that their translation process is efficient and effective. |\n| Supported Content Types and Roles/Permissions | Expedia supports a wide range of content types, including website content, marketing materials, and legal documents. They also have specific roles and permissions |", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [8420, 374, 279, 16148, 315, 279, 14468, 1882, 315, 7787, 4495, 1447, 91, 80053, 760, 71287, 9248, 91, 12448, 760, 12448, 9248, 91, 80820, 27745, 760, 7787, 4495, 5711, 264, 10601, 315, 8622, 2022, 323, 52304, 14830, 304, 862, 14468, 1882, 13, 2379, 614, 264, 57883, 2083, 429, 28872, 279, 14468, 1882, 11, 714, 1083, 614, 2205, 7263, 311, 3705, 3151, 13604, 13, 9248, 91, 39613, 760, 7787, 4495, 702, 264, 12235, 52304, 2083, 8480, 369, 18150, 279, 14468, 1882, 13, 2379, 1083, 975, 448, 9250, 14468, 13304, 369, 3654, 15459, 13, 9248, 91, 350, 4826, 760, 7787, 4495, 5711, 264, 38041, 9551, 739, 320, 51, 4826, 8, 311, 10091, 323, 68611, 862, 14468, 1882, 13, 2379, 990, 264, 31689, 2319, 315, 14653, 1163, 5553, 369, 419, 7428, 13, 9248, 91, 19087, 760, 12960, 38041, 320, 8505, 8, 374, 1483, 553, 7787, 4495, 311, 3705, 1550, 66768, 11, 3347, 2268, 8773, 2213, 13, 2379, 990, 2526, 19087, 21106, 7881, 304, 35902, 11, 438, 1632, 438, 4843, 24031, 19087, 12565, 13, 9248, 91, 23975, 760, 7787, 4495, 5711, 38041, 86616, 320, 22034, 8, 311, 3553, 8597, 24531, 2213, 323, 25978, 432, 979, 5871, 13, 2379, 614, 264, 3460, 23975, 4625, 429, 374, 1483, 311, 5978, 28137, 323, 4628, 705, 279, 14468, 1882, 13, 9248, 91, 36241, 40069, 760, 7787, 4495, 74662, 862, 14468, 1882, 4