INFO 03-13 07:55:21 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-e2e989aeb221400882042166eafbb942-0: prompt: 'I apologize for the confusion. It seems that the `metric` method is no longer available in the latest version of the `im4java` library.\n\nHere\'s an updated version of the `areImagesEqual` function that should work:\n```kotlin\nimport org.im4java.core.CompareCmd\nimport org.im4java.core.IMOperation\nimport java.io.File\n\nfun areImagesEqual(image1Path: String, image2Path: String): Boolean {\n    val compare = CompareCmd()\n    val operation = IMOperation().addImage(image1Path).addImage(image2Path).metric("AE").appendRawArgs("-fuzz", "10%")\n    compare.run(operation)\n    return compare.getExitValue() == 0\n}\n```\nThis function takes two image paths as input and returns true if the images are the same (i.e., have the same content), and false otherwise. It does this by running the ImageMagick `compare` command using the `CompareCmd` class, which compares two images and returns the difference metric between them. In this updated version, we\'re also using the `-fuzz` option to allow for small differences between the images (in this case, up to 10%). If the exit value of the `compare` command is 0, the images are the same.\n\nNote that ImageMagick requires the installation of its command-line tools, so you need to make sure that they are installed on your system and available in your `PATH`.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [40, 36879, 369, 279, 21340, 13, 1084, 4977, 429, 279, 1565, 15903, 63, 1714, 374, 902, 5021, 2500, 304, 279, 5535, 2319, 315, 279, 1565