INFO 03-13 07:55:23 logger.py:39] Received request cmpl-0cd2f561f8834e658d12b954a27fa093-0: prompt: 'Apologies for the confusion. Since U-Net has skip connections, we need a custom approach to implement pipeline parallelism. Here\'s an updated version of the `PipelineParallelUNet` class that handles skip connections properly:\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom torch.distributed.pipeline.sync import Pipe, PipeRpcWrapper\n\nclass PipelineParallelUNet(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, in_channels=3, devices=None):\n        super(PipelineParallelUNet, self).__init__()\n        self.devices = devices if devices else [torch.device("cuda:0"), torch.device("cuda:1"), torch.device("cuda:2"), torch.device("cuda:3")]\n\n        self.encoder1 = PipeRpcWrapper(Encoder(in_channels, 64).to(self.devices[0]), chunks=8)\n        self.encoder2 = PipeRpcWrapper(Encoder(64, 128).to(self.devices[1]), chunks=8)\n        self.encoder3 = PipeRpcWrapper(Encoder(128, 256).to(self.devices[2]), chunks=8)\n        self.encoder4 = PipeRpcWrapper(Encoder(256, 512).to(self.devices[3]), chunks=8)\n\n        self.decoder1 = PipeRpcWrapper(Decoder(512, 256).to(self.devices[2]), chunks=8)\n        self.decoder2 = PipeRpcWrapper(Decoder(256, 128).to(self.devices[1]), chunks=8)\n        self.decoder3 = PipeRpcWrapper(Decoder(128, 64).to(self.devices[0]), chunks=8)\n\n        self.final = nn.Conv2d(64, in_channels, kernel_size=1).to(self.devices[0])\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        x = x.to(self.devices[0])\n\n        x1, skip1 = self.encoder1(x)\n        x2, skip2 = self.encoder2(x1)\n        x3, skip3 = self.encoder3(x2)\n        x4, _ = self.encoder4(x3)\n\n        x5 = self.decoder1(x4, skip3)\n        x6 = self.decoder2(x5, skip2)\n        x7 = self.decoder3(x6, skip1)\n\n        x_out = self.final(x7)\n        return x_out\n```\nIn this version, we use the `PipeRpcWrapper` to wrap each module separately, which allows us to manually handle the skip connections during the forward pass. This approach will work with pipeline parallelism while preserving the skip connections. Note that `PipeRpcWrapper` is not part of the official PyTorch API, so you may need to implement it based on your requirements. The above code assumes that `PipeRpcWrapper` takes care of the pipeline parallelism for individual layers.', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=True, max_tokens=256, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: [10611, 9090, 369, 279, 21340, 13, 8704, 547, 12, 6954, 702, 10706, 13234, 11, 582, 1184, 264, 2526, 5486, 311, 4211, 15301, 15279, 2142, 13, 5692, 594, 458, 6049, 2319, 315, 279, 1565, 34656, 16547, 1861, 295, 63, 536, 429, 13469, 10706, 13234, 10277, 510, 73594, 12669, 198, 474, 7834, 198, 474, 7834, 19900, 438, 10883, 198, 1499, 7834, 950, 25146, 57733, 30712, 1159, 27805, 11, 27805, 60248, 11542, 271, 1040, 40907, 16547, 1861, 295, 33478, 26958, 982, 262, 707, 1304, 2327, 3804, 721, 11, 304, 19291, 28, 18, 11, 7611, 5856, 982, 286, 2256, 5304, 8790, 16547, 1861, 295, 11, 656, 20390, 2327, 32616, 286, 656, 78914, 284, 7611, 421, 7611, 770, 508, 27414, 18355, 445, 33926, 25, 15, 3975, 7834, 18355, 445, 33926, 25, 16, 3975, 7834, 18355, 445, 33926, 25, 17, 3975, 7834, 18355, 445, 33926, 25, 18, 72389, 286, 656, 69042, 16, 284, 27805, 60248, 11542, 7, 19921, 5900, 19291, 11, 220, 21, 19, 568, 983, 1193, 78914, 58, 15, 9719, 26757, 28, 23, 340, 286, 656, 69042, 17, 284, 27805, 60248, 11542, 7, 19921, 7, 21, 19, 11, 220, 16, 17, 23, 568, 983, 1193, 78914, 58, 16, 9719, 26757, 28, 23, 340, 286, 656, 69042, 18, 284, 27805, 60248, 11542, 7, 19921, 7, 16, 17, 23, 11, 220, 17, 20, 21, 568, 983, 1193, 7